{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms","id":41641,"title":"Alternate Watchtowers/Supernal Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-03T04:35:10-08:00","id":41641,"title":"Alternate Watchtowers/Supernal Realms","content":"So are there any alternative Supernal Realms/Watch Towers in the Books or made by fans? I'm curious, I thought I remembered a project for making a realm for each combination of Arcana.<br /> <br /> Has anyone used them in games? I don't see a problem with doing so frankly, particularly if the whole cabal of PCs are each from one of these unknown paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T05:32:37-08:00","id":41654,"title":"","content":"There's one Supernal World, seen through five different interpretations.<br /> <br /> That said, Left Hand Path has both of the hinted at alternatives in it.<br /> <br /> A Tremere legend of a sixth Watchtower of the Soul that would encompass all the existing Paths and is either a) a delusion b) a warped interpretation of a Lower Depth c) in the abyss or d) related to a Bound - that is, it was in the Supernal, but has been removed.<br /> <br /> The five Abyssal Ziggurats, anti-Watchtowers set in Abyssal worlds that resemble elementally-flipped perversions of the Path Realms, that mid-ranking Scelesti journey to. For example, the Anti-Aether is the flooded ocean-floor wreckage of the Nephilim's cities - the cold, dark symbolism of power utterly destroyed as the mirror to the Aether.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T06:16:53-08:00","id":41666,"title":"","content":"The Mage Chronicler's Guide talks about some alternatives to how Paths work, and then explores the implications of that in the Supernal. Is it a new Watchtower that heralding in a new era for the Awakened, or a harbinger of Abyssal supremacy? Are there dozens of Watchtowers, of each Arcanum combination, and thus a myriad of independent realms within the Supernal? It talks about these and a few other takes.<br /> <br /> My rule of thumb, though, especially with the WoD, is that if there's a, &quot;What If?&quot; idea you have about the setting then use it! Maybe people in-setting believe it but it isn't true? Or maybe it now is true and turns the world upside-down.<br /> <br /> Your PCs are watching a group of Sleepers who have been groomed to Awaken for years and then, suddenly, they all Awaken the same night and they all traveled to a hitherto unknown Watchtower. Are they infect by the Abyss? Turned into Banishers? Maybe your PC is one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T06:17:51-08:00","id":41667,"title":"","content":"The Chronicler's Guide (I think) also suggest new Watchtowers (a.k.a alternative views of the Supernal World), like the path of Djinn and the suggest for a &quot;supernal realm of vampires&quot;. There is also the False Awakening which could be used as inspiration (if you drop the part were you are exploded in the end, of course)<br /> <br /> Edit- ninjad..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-03-2014, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T06:26:10-08:00","id":41670,"title":"","content":"In the Mage Chronicle's Guide, there is the Watchtower of Brass and flame. That was kinda neat. I think there was a False Path in Intruders as well, a kind of Abyssal disease that faked being a tower.<br /> <br /> But as far the Fan project goes...you're going to be more specific. I remember no fewer than 6 or 7 attempts... Including 3 on rpg.net, though I can only find links for <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?688139-M-tAw-The-Other-Watchtowers\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?364013-nMage-The-Supernal-Infinite\" target=\"_blank\">two</a>.The rest I recall were in the WW forums. Checking the Archives now...I do recall that Dataweaver did a really cool take though, with 5 alternates...<br /> <br /> Edit: Found some! DW talk's about adding Leagices to them <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default1130-2.html?g=posts&amp;t=78620\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. His original thread is <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultf443-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=31608\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Another DW one is <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default3d4b.html?g=posts&amp;t=80461\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, noted for it's visuals.<br /> Will return if/when I find more","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 01-03-2014, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:08:53-08:00","id":41690,"title":"","content":"I worked up a set of five designed to complement the standard five, and posted them on the <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultf443-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=31608\" target=\"_blank\">old forums</a> and on the old Wiki. Here\u2019s a summary:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Epikrateia</span></b><br /> Sorcerers on the Path of Mastery; scions of the Watchtower of the Brazen Lamp in the Realm of Mount Qaf, Kingdom of the Living Elements, Abode of the Djinn.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Path Attribute:</i> Resolve<br /> <i>Ruling Arcana:</i> Forces and Spirit<br /> <i>Inferior Arcanum:</i> Prime<br /> <i>Nimbus:</i> &quot;Inflaming&quot;<br /> <i>Tarot:</i> the Emperor<br /> <i>Common Virtue and Vice:</i> Justice and Wrath<br /> <i>Existing Legacies:</i> Clavicularius, Tamers of Sands<br /> <i>New Legacies:</i> Djinn Summoners?</div>This is a slightly modified version of the Watchtower of Brass and Flame from the <b>Mage Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>. I changed the name to conform to the naming scheme used by every other Watchtower (but tried to keep the essence of \u201cBrass and Flame\u201d in the new name), and I changed the Path Attribute from Composure to Resolve to reflect the more forceful personalities I envisioned them having.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chrysopos</span></b><br /> Alchemists on the Path of Excellence,<br /> Scions of the Watchtower of the Copper Mallet in the Realm of Utopia,<br /> Kingdom of Perfection, Abode of Archetypes.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Path Attribute:</i> Composure<br /> <i>Ruling Arcana:</i> Matter and Prime<br /> <i>Inferior Arcanum:</i> Fate<br /> <i>Nimbus:</i> &quot;Perfectionist&quot;<br /> <i>Tarot:</i> Temperance<br /> <i>Common Virtue and Vice:</i> Prudence and Greed<br /> <i>Existing Legacies:</i> Uncrowned Kings, Daksha, Scions of God, Transhuman Engineers, Tamers of Iron, Forge Masters<br /> <i>New Legacies:</i> a Summoner Legacy that draws upon \u201cPlatonic Archetypes\u201d of things.</div>The theme of this Path was intended to encompass all mystics centered on the notion of magical items, not just practitioners of Supernal Alchemy \u2014 though they tend to excel in that, too. Prime was selected for the alchemists to represent the raw building blocks of reality, and because of its usefulness in working with Imbued Items of all sorts.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Palinoros</span></b><br /> Druids on the Path of Balance, Scions of the Watchtower of the Wooden Chalice in the Realm of Yggdrasil,<br /> Kingdom of Seasons, Abode of G\u00e6ans</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Path Attribute:</i> Resolve<br /> <i>Ruling Arcana:</i> Life and Death<br /> <i>Inferior Arcanum:</i> Time<br /> <i>Nimbus:</i> &quot;Patient&quot;<br /> <i>Tarot:</i> Wheel of Fortune<br /> <i>Common Virtue and Vice:</i> Temperance and Envy<br /> <i>Existing Legacies:</i> Orphans of Proteus, Walkers in the Mists, Sodality of the Tor, Dreamspeakers, Tamers of Trees, Tamers of Blood?, Thread Cutters<br /> <i>New Legacies:</i></div>I wanted to build a Path out of the pairing of Life and Death, and took European paganism (particularly the druids of the British Islands) as my inspiration. \u201cG\u00e6ans\u201d is a vague term for its denizens, and I was never really happy with it. At various points, I considered serpents, Ent-like tree-people, and Dryads as candidates; but I never settled on a single, consistent set of imagery for the inhabitants of the Kingdom of Seasons. <br /> <br /> This Path differs from the Thyrsus in that it\u2019s more of a \u201cCircle of Life\u201d thing than an \u201ceat or be eaten\u201d thing: nature green in growth and decay rather than nature red in tooth and claw.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">C\u00e6lum</span></b><br /> Astrologers on the Path of Discovery,<br /> Scions of the Watchtower of the Hermium Mirror in the Realm of the Firmament,<br /> Kingdom of Vision, Abode of Stars</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Path Attribute:</i> Composure<br /> <i>Ruling Arcana:</i> Space and Fate<br /> <i>Inferior Arcanum:</i> Life<br /> <i>Nimbus:</i> &quot;Watchful&quot;<br /> <i>Tarot:</i> the Star<br /> <i>Common Virtue and Vice:</i> Faith and Greed<br /> <i>Existing Legacies:</i>Subtle Ones, Threnodists, Tamers of Light, Sphinxes, Thrice-Great, House of Ariadne?<br /> <i>New Legacies:</i> a Summoner Legacy that calls the Stars down for guidance.</div>The C\u00e6lum were very loosely based off of the historical antecedents of <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>\u2019s Void Engineers: the Void Seekers and the Celestial Masters. Fate is for when they look to the heavens for guidance about the future; Space is for when they look to the heavens for guidance about the world around them. The Stars than inhabit the Firmament are generally humanoid figures, inspired by the stars in C.S. Lewis\u2019 Narnia series (esp. <i>Voyage of the Dawn Treader</i>); it\u2019s a notion that has also been used by Neil Gaiman in <i>Stardust</i> and <i>Endless Nights</i>.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hieraoidos</span></b><br /> Bards on the Path of Enlightenment,<br /> Scions of the Watchtower of the Tin Flute in the Realm of the Akasha,<br /> Kingdom of Stories, Abode of Zeitgeists</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Path Attribute:</i> Resolve<br /> <i>Ruling Arcana:</i> Time and Mind<br /> <i>Inferior Arcanum:</i> Space<br /> <i>Nimbus:</i> &quot;Iconic&quot;<br /> <i>Tarot:</i> the Magician<br /> <i>Common Virtue and Vice:</i> Charity and Sloth<br /> <i>Existing Legacies:</i> Perfected Adepts, Daoine?, House of Ariadne?, Pygmalions, Stone Scribes, Skalds<br /> <i>New Legacies:</i> Ecstatics who channel Zeitgeists</div>Nearly every time I\u2019ve seen someone do a Legacy or Path featuring Time, it has been forward-looking; so I wanted to do something aligned more with the past. These folk are based on celtic bards and nordic skalds; they\u2019re storytellers, entertainers, and keepers of ancient wisdom. I drew imagery and concepts from <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>\u2019s Akashic Brotherhood (for the Akashic Record) and the Cult of Ecstasy (for the Zeitgeists).<br /> <br /> The <i>Existing Legacies</i> are there if you want to co-opt any of the existing Legacies for use with the new Paths instead of the existing ones. They\u2019re a work in progress. The <i>New Legacies</i> are ideas for Legacies that build on aspects of the Path\u2019s imagery and do not already exist. I\u2019d like at least two per Path, not counting Elemental Tamers or Summoners-style Legacies.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> latest version found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-07-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:01:45-08:00","id":41718,"title":"","content":"In the game I'm in right now, we're using the concept that the watchtowers are just a beacon and you can possibly Awaken to other &quot;regions&quot; of a given supernal realm (although it is uncommon). My mage landed in a particularly magical part of the Primal Wild and got Life/Prime ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:44:11-08:00","id":41741,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the \u201cWarlocks of Arcadia\u201d hack in <b>Mage Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>.<br /> <br /> The idea is that Path and Realm are decoupled, with Path determining your Subtle Arcanum and Realm determining your Gross Arcanum. I remember working up something for this, too, with each Realm having five Kingdoms in it corresponding to the five Paths and each Path having five titles corresponding to the five Realms. I posted it on the Wiki, though; so it\u2019s currently MIA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2014, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:50:22-08:00","id":41746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41741#post41741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the \u201cWarlocks of Arcadia\u201d hack in <b>Mage Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes! That's what it was. I couldn't remember where we got the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:57:27-08:00","id":41799,"title":"","content":"Awesome you guys I'll give them all a look. DataWeaver what is the Inferior Arcanum of the Palinoros? Its hard to guess these, is it Time? Or Spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T10:06:24-08:00","id":41803,"title":"","content":"Sorry; I somehow skipped that while reformatting everything. It\u2019s Time: their association with cycles (e.g., birth, death, and rebirth, or the progression of the seasons) means that time is something they generally don\u2019t try to manipulate.<br /> <br /> Note that among the Ten Watchtowers, every Arcanum shows up twice as a Ruling Arcanum and once as an Inferior Arcanum. That is, there\u2019s no overlap between the original five Paths\u2019s Inferior Arcana and my five new Paths\u2019 Inferior Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2014, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T10:15:42-08:00","id":41809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41803#post41803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry; I somehow skipped that while reformatting everything. It\u2019s Time: their association with cycles (e.g., birth, death, and rebirth, or the progression of the seasons) means that time is something they generally don\u2019t try to manipulate.<br /> <br /> Note that among the Ten Watchtowers, every Arcanum shows up twice as a Ruling Arcanum and once as an Inferior Arcanum. That is, there\u2019s no overlap between the original five Paths\u2019s Inferior Arcana and my five new Paths\u2019 Inferior Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so proud I got that one with my first try! I was not really confident in my savvy on the subject!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T10:27:10-08:00","id":41818,"title":"","content":"Here's what I came up with on this.<br /> <br /> In this alternate cosmology, there are still five known Realms in the Supernal World; but each Realm has within it five Kingdoms, each with its own Watchtower. As such, there are 25 Paths to which a mage can Awaken. The Watchtowers presented in the corebook are considered the &quot;core&quot; of the Realm in question. The two primary Arcana of that Path are the dominating influences on the landscape. However, as you move away from that central point, the Gross Arcanum in that direction begins to influence the landscape, but the Subtle Arcanum still dominates.<br /> <br /> <b>Realm of the Aether</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Aether, the guiding principle is <i>Faith</i>. Faith can move mountains, change lives, and shine in the dark when all other lights have been extinguished. The inhabitants of the Aether will always try to encourage the mage to become that light, but one man\u2019s \u201clight\u201d is not always the same as his neighbor\u2019s. Some will take strength from their Faith and use it to reach for the greatest heights (Path of the Mighty). Some will use their Faith in the service others and give what they can for the greater good (Path of Sacrifice). Some will apply their Faith with the greatest of ease for the maximum effect, and find themselves rewarded (Path of Immortality). Some will use that Faith to unite that which is separated and forge chains to link them all together (Path of Unity). Some will simply ride the Universal Cycle with joy in their hearts and have Faith that they will see it through to the Great End (Path of Eternity).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Celestial Spheres<br /> Abode of Angels, Watchtower of the Gold Key<br /> <b>Obrimos:</b> the Theurges on the Path of Might<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Death<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of World Trees<br /> Abode of Dryads, Watchtower of the Oaken Sickle<br /> <b>Verbenae:</b> the Druids on the Path of Sacrifice<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Spirit<br /> With great trees stretching down into the mist and high into the clouds, the Kingdom of World Trees awaits those who would choose Sacrifice as the way to the heavens. Those who visit here will find themselves leaping among the branches and leaves, risking a fall at every step. The Dryads will not help the would-be mage; in fact, they will ask him for assistance. They will beg for water for their drying leaves, ask for help in removing vines and weeds from their tiny, tree-top gardens. Only those who stop and help, and can keep their balance, will be guided to the branches of a great oak. Through a door carved into the side in the shape of a sickle, they can enter the Watchtower and leave their name in this sacred grove.<br /> Relation to Center - Down<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Effortless Action<br /> Abode of Celestial Masters, Watchtower of the Jade Crucible<br /> <b>Athanatos:</b> the Alchemists on the Path of Immortality<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Fate<br /> Well below the crashing skies of the Aether is a series of furnaces and crucibles, surrounded by huts containing all manner of materials. Waiting here for the would-be mage are the Celestial Masters, willing to offer guidance to those who ask the right questions. Many have come here and begun to throw items into the crucibles and furnaces, hoping to forge themselves the right substance to grant them their wishes of power and immortality. Fewer still have known to search for the Jade Crucible, but this does not grant them the knowledge of the correct materials to use. Only by taking the time to study with one of the old Masters can one hope to find the way. Only by understanding how simple it really is will the Watchtower be revealed.<br /> Relation to Center - Under<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Divine Simplicity<br /> Abode of Sefirot, Watchtower of the Stardust Chain<br /> <b>Halusis:</b> the Geomancers on the Path of Unity<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Death<br /> Within the Realm of Aether, there exists a great chain, linking all the way up to the clouds. If one were to begin to ascend this chain, they would find more chains going off in other directions, and those links having yet more chains. If the would-be mage can take a step back to see, they will find those chains going in all directions, linking everything together in a massive web. At different points, many chains will link together in a seeming knot of connected things; all the chains for animals &amp; plants will connect as all things living, all the chains for lust and envy and wrath and greed will come together as a collection of vices. At the greatest nexus points are the Sefirot, representing the highest ideals and greatest concepts. By following the chains of the Sefirot, the would-be mage can climb this web to the Watchtower and leave their name on the wall of stardust.<br /> Relation to Center - Below<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Righteous Order<br /> Abode of Avatars, Watchtower of the Lotus Table<br /> <b>Ogygios:</b> the Channelers on the Path of Eternity<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Death<br /> On a great, calm pool of water, there are endless lotus blossoms, each floating upon the surface and dancing to their own tunes. Some of the blossoms will collect together and all dance in harmony. Others will separate after a long time of dancing together, and begin to drift away, or sink beneath the surface altogether. New blossoms will break the surface and begin to dance, either alone or with others. The would-be mage who comes here has no one and nothing to interact with, until they understand what they are seeing. Each blossom is a soul; each collection is a circle of friends and family. When they drift away or sink, the circle is broken. Death or disorder has taken someone away. When a new blossom appears, a new soul has entered the world. Once the Awakening soul has grasped this, an Avatar will join him and show him to the Watchtower.<br /> Relation to Center - Beneath</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of Arcadia</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Arcadia, the guiding principle is <i>Bravery</i>. As the old saying goes, \u201cFortune Favors the Brave.\u201d Dealing with Fate, in all its forms, requires a mage to take chances, face changes, and trust that the outcome will be what was meant to happen. Arcadia will test a would-be mage\u2019s mettle with warnings of danger, portents of doom, and threats of death; those who go on to face the tests and brave the dangers have better understanding of Fate and how it works for them, against them, and with them. Some will treat Fate as the coming storm, full of chaos and energy, but better for its passing (Path of Thunder). Some will see the winding up of living beings and happenstance and they will not hesitate to cut it when necessary (Path of Destiny). Some will see Fate as something that can be hammered and molded into shape, forcing it into a forged destiny (Path of Artifacts). Some will want to know all the paths Fate has laid out and see all the possibilities, even if it destroys their minds (Path of Discovery). Some will simply let the tides of Fate and Time push &amp; pull them where it will and trust to luck (Path of Thistle).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Enchantment<br /> Abode of the Fae, Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn<br /> <b>Acanthus:</b> the Enchanters on the Path of Thistle<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Forces<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Storms<br /> Abode of Great Ravens, Watchtower of the Frozen Spear<br /> <b>Magi:</b> the Wizards on the Path of Thunder<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Space<br /> The Watchtower of the Frozen Spear stands at the peak of the highest mountain of Arcadia, stretching above even the tallest tree of the greatest forest of the Realm, surrounded by vast seas of snow and ice. Perched upon its many peaks are the Great Ravens who call this region home. They wait for would-be mages to approach the Watchtower and bring down storms and clouds of black wings upon those who would enter. The path for anyone who could call themselves a wizard is difficult, and the Path of Foresight requires that a Wizard be prepared for hardship and sudden changes in fortune. If successful, a mage can carve their name into the handle of the Frozen Spear with one of the many icicles hanging from the arches of the tower\u2019s doorways.<br /> Relation from Center - Up<br /> <br /> Kingdom of the Turning Wheel<br /> Abode of the Norns, Watchtower of the Obsidian Knife<br /> <b>Moirae:</b> the Fate-Weavers on the Path of Destiny<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Matter<br /> As a would-be mage wanders through the forests of Arcadia, approaching the mountains takes the visitor through a region that is strange even by the standards of this Realm. At first, the trees appear to be a birch of some kind, with white bark and red leaves and vines. Upon closer inspection, they are found to be gigantic bones with the leaves and vines being pieces of flesh still attached to them. This is a place built on the bodies of Giants and Titans, cut up and stripped bare to make of Forest of Flesh &amp; Bone. The only inhabitants of this Kingdom are 3 women; call them Norns, Fates, or the Weird Sisters. It doesn\u2019t matter to them, but they will test a visitor before allowing entrance to the Watchtower. Passing the test grants the mage a pair of shears which they can use to hack their name into the thick, black walls of the Watchtower.<br /> Relation from Center - Across<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Mines<br /> Abode of Dwarfs, Watchtower of the Diamond Chisel<br /> <b>Techne:</b> the Craftsmen on the Path of Artifacts<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Space<br /> Doting the landscape of the Enchanted Forests of Arcadia are several great holes in the ground. These holes will lead to great caves and vast mines where the Dwarfs make their homes and craft their enchanted items. The Dwarfs have great smiths and forges working at all times, day and night are irrelevant under the ground. The powerful artifacts they create lie on rows and columns of shelves, well maintained and polished, but one stands out among all others \u2013 the Diamond Chisel. This tool must be taken before the would-be mage can continue, and the Dwarfs will only allow those who show some skill in crafting to take it with them. Once obtained, the visitor travels deep within one of the great caverns to the Watchtower, gleaming bright with clear crystal. When they have etched their name into the Watchtower with the Chisel, they can truly claim the title of Craftsman.<br /> Relation from Center - Below<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Revelation<br /> Abode of Nebulas, Watchtower of the Opal Door<br /> <b>Eureka:</b> the Astrologers on the Path of Discovery<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Matter<br /> High above, in the skies of Arcadia, lays the Boundless Firmament. In these endless reaches, all possibilities are waiting to be found. Each potential outcome is a pinpoint of light against a backdrop of black. Reaching for the stars here is not a metaphor, but a reality. Each star contains new knowledge, and with that knowledge comes the potential to know more and do more. Each new discovery leads to another, but that is another star to chase, another bright point for the Astrologer to follow, and they simply do not have the time. The Watchtower of the Opal Door, the brightest spot on the horizon, pulls potential mages in like a white dwarf star. Here, they must burn their name into the door before too long or fall back to earth, forever denied the Boundless Firmament again.<br /> Relation from Center - Above</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of Pandemonium</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Pandemonium, the guiding principle is <i>Purification</i>. The creatures of the Realm are there to expose the flaws of the soul and to force improvement within the soul. They tempt, they torture, they steal, they punish and they abuse; All in the name of turning the would-be mage into a soul worthy to hold the power of magic. Pandemonium will accept no weaklings or cowards. Some will be tempted to Glutton themselves and simply take what is given, but they must move on to find the Watchtower (Path of Determination). Some will be tempted with a Lust for everything a body could desire, but only by focusing will they find the Watchtower (Path of Introspection). Some will see the strength of other souls and Envy them and wish to Greedily take what they see, but only by forging their own soul will they find the Watchtower (Path of Forging). Some will be Prideful and try to hide their flaws, but if they will be open and lay bare, they will be admitted into the Watchtower (Path of Scourging). Some will find they are harassed and tempted to give into Sloth, but those who learn patience will discover the Watchtower (Path of Observance).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Nightmares<br /> Abode of Demons, Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet<br /> <b>Mastigos:</b> the Warlocks on the Path of Scourging<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Matter<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Abundance<br /> Abode of Harpies, Watchtower of the Bone Trident<br /> <b>Satur:</b> the Devoted on the Path of Determination<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Spirit<br /> Nestled in a valley in the Mountains of Abundance, the Watchtower of the Bone Trident sits. All the things one could ever want in life are there, piled in heaps to create this mountain range. Seemingly endless tracts of junk &amp; gadgets, food &amp; clothes, positions &amp; people make up the mountains. The mountains will rise and fall as their importance shifts based on the souls who travel through the mess. Would-be mages who travel here are free to dive within the mounds and take what they can when they can, but the Harpies who live atop these mountains are only too happy to teach them a lesson about what is truly precious \u2013 the soul. Anyone who grabs up the abundant materials lying about will find themselves in the clutches of a Harpie, carried far away from the Watchtower and dumped into another pile. Only those who can remain determined enough to go past all the garbage can finally be called a Devoted mage of the Bone Trident.<br /> Relation to Center - Above<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Temptations<br /> Abode of Sirens, Watchtower of the Banyan Staff<br /> <b>Askesis:</b> the Yogis on the Path of Introspection<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Matter<br /> Upon a rolling hill of dried grass, under an overcast sky, there\u2019s a series of tables and bed and chests, containing every manner of food, drink, pleasure and distraction created since the beginning of time; anything and everything someone could possibly desire to fulfill their bodily needs. Drifting across their Plain of Desire are the calls of the Sirens, telling the visitor to this Kingdom all about how great it will feel and how easy it is to give in to their temptations. Many a would-be mage has succumbed to their calls, and found himself back in the Fallen World, still hungry and unAwakened. For those who focus past all these temptations, beyond stands the Watchtower of the Banyan Staff, where a mage may carve their name into the trunks of the trees.<br /> Relation to Center - Across<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Transmutation<br /> Abode of Golems, Watchtower of the Copper Mallet<br /> <b>Telchines:</b> the Artificers on the Path of Forging<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Death<br /> Deep in the caves of Pandemonium is a forge like no other. Here, it\u2019s not metal that is worked, but souls. The visitor who is drawn here already knows their flaws, and wants them burned out or hammered out. He doesn\u2019t care, because he loathes those flaws, and wants the strength he sees in others. But the Golems do not give him what he wants, it must be earned. The would-be mage must place his soul upon the anvil, with mallet in hand, and perform the task himself. When a mage can forge his soul into the desired form, then can he approach the Watchtower to leave his name within its walls.<br /> Relation to Center - Under<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Distractions<br /> Abode of Goblins, Watchtower of the Marble Labyrinth<br /> <b>Perispao:</b> the Mystics on the Path of Observance<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Forces<br /> Contained within the Kingdom of Distractions are endless chambers filled with shining baubles, grating music, pungent smells, and rough surfaces. Many a would-be mage has lost his way completely in the continuing stretch of passages and chambers, too disoriented to tell which way he\u2019s been and which way is out. Adding to those distractions are the Goblins, who scurry about the passageways and through the various chambers tossing objects at the visitor, or destroying any attempts at marking their way. Those who can be patient, who can focus their minds and take their time, will eventually find the center of this maze. Within this waiting oubliette, the mage-to-be must slowly form their name in the walls with nothing more than their imagination.<br /> Relation to Center - Down</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of the Primal Wild</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of the Primal Wilds, the guiding principle is <i>Primitive</i>. Not in the sense of under-developed, but in the sense of being straight-forward and uncomplicated. The beings which exist here are clear and distinct about what they are and what they do. They don\u2019t talk in riddles, they don\u2019t play games, and they don\u2019t contemplate their nature. They exist as they are and they react to visiting souls within that paradigm: hunter or hunted, pack or herd, master or servant. Some will come to this Realm and see their place as a master of ephemera (Path of Authority). Some will come here and exalt in the headiness of a place full of life (Path of Ecstasy). Some will come here and form their own world out of the dirt (Path of Sculpting). Some will come to thrill in the hunt and the freedom to run over the open spaces (Path of Predators). Some will come here and bow down to the beings that live here, letting themselves be taken and open to everything (Path of Servitude).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Totems<br /> Abode of Beasts, Watchtower of the Stone Book<br /> <b>Thyrsus:</b> the Shamans on the Path of Ecstasy<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Mind<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Burning Sands<br /> Abode of Djinn, Watchtower of the Brass Torch<br /> <b>Exousi:</b> the Sorcerers on the Path of Authority<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Prime<br /> Within the ravished garden of the Primal Wild is the Kingdom of Burning Sands. The Djinn drift and fly through here, creating vast winds and sandstorms. Lightning splits the skies and thunder splits the ears almost constantly. The Djinn are angry at the ruins they are left. The would-be mage has but one option to deal with them \u2013 take command. Only a soul who is willing and able to control the Djinn will be able to see his way through the sand and find the Watchtower, burning his name into the walls with his command of the smokeless flames.<br /> Relation to Center - Higher<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Mud<br /> Abode of Gargoyles, Watchtower of the Clay Statue<br /> <b>Peitho:</b> the Binders on the Path of Sculpting<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Space<br /> In the damp earth of the Primal Wilds, the Gargoyles wait for a new creator. Each visiting soul encounters these creatures, waiting for orders or for the generative act to begin. The souls here seem compelled to create something out of the mud and clay around their feet. Once a would-be mage begins to create a new gargoyle, the others will turn their backs and guard, watching for any who would interfere with the creation process. The completed gargoyle must have life imbued into it, through the force of will of the Sculptor, binding it into servitude. Once this has been completed, the newly created gargoyle can be instructed to lead the way to the Watchtower, where it will claw its master\u2019s name into the walls.<br /> Relation to Center - Down<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Mountain Tundra<br /> Abode of Wendigo, Watchtower of Antler Bow<br /> <b>Necans:</b> the Hunters on the Path of Predators<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Life<br /> The Primal Wilds are host to vast, open reaches of mountain and arctic tundra, dotted with herd animals of many kinds: caribou, musk ox, mammoths, antelope, bison, moose, elk; anything capable of existing in the chilled reaches of this realm. Running across this Kingdom in great packs are the Wendigo, spirits who have turned to cannibalism and begun feeding on other spirits. Once, they were herd animals like the others here, then the first souls came and showed them how to hunt, and they were forever changed. Would-be mages attracted to this Kingdom are here to join in that hunt, drawing power from the spirits they bring down and consume. Once a soul has covered many, many miles and forged weapons of the hunt, they will find a great Watchtower to scratch their name into with an antler or stone weapon.<br /> Relation to Center - Across<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Great Rivers<br /> Abode of Loa, Watchtower of the Ivory Horse<br /> <b>Houngan:</b> the Mediums on the Path of Servitude<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Mind<br /> n a place where the waters of the Primal Wilds collect into rivers, there dwell spirits who do not feel the need to serve the souls who visit here, nor do they wish to work with them. These spirits see beyond there here and now; they see far off into the unwritten future or back into the well-worn past. The souls of the would-be mages that visit here are just drops of rain in the Great Rivers of time. The souls who come here are not the masters, they are the servants. The Loa, for all their knowledge, envy one thing: sensation. Those willing to give themselves over to the Loa, even for such a brief period as their Awakening, will find this moment stretched into an eternity. The Loa will take their time with the pleasures of sensation, but in the end, they will always leave the visiting soul at the foot of the Watchtower, where they may leave their name and claim the power they have earned with their servitude.<br /> Relation to Center \u2013 Beneath</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of Stygia</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Stygia, the guiding principle is <i>Acceptance</i>; Acceptance of one\u2019s fates, of their state of being, of their place in the Universe, of their flaws, and of themselves. Stygia accepts those who come to its Watchtowers with open arms, open hearts and open minds. The inhabitants of the Realm will never, ever interfere with a visitor\u2019s wanderings through the Realm. Neither will they guide, push, pull or direct anyone to a particular Watchtower. The soul of a mage in Stygia will drift until the natural pull of a Watchtower draws them in. Those who Awaken within Stygia have seen Death, and they understand it\u2019s place in the scheme of things, and they accept it as well as their own place. Some choose to fight, despite the knowledge of futility, but find nobility in the fight (Path of Strife). Some choose to help balance out the natural ebb &amp; flow between life &amp; death, loving each thing and crying at their passing (Path of Tears). Some concern themselves with the transition and transformation from one state to another, and help to ease that transition (Path of Doom). Some simply wait for the end, watching for signs and making their life as comfortable as possible in the meantime (Path of Oblivion). Some do their best to see what\u2019s coming and to either help it along or turn it aside, but they know that it is simply a matter of time (Path of Inevitability).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Crypts<br /> Abode of Shades, Watchtower of the Lead Coin<br /> <b>Moros:</b> the Necromancers on the Path of Doom<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Spirit<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Fallen Warriors<br /> Abode of the Valkyries, Watchtower of the Ebony Shield<br /> <b>Keres:</b> the Soul-Collectors on the Path of Strife<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Life<br /> Towering above the Hall of Valhalla, placed upon the storm clouds of Odin, stands the Watchtower of the Ebony Shield, surrounded by constant mist and illuminated only by the lightning arcing though the clouds it stands on. Here, upon their winged steeds, the Valkyries spiral and swoop through the clouds and congregate within the tower, waiting for the next great warrior to enter and etch his or her name into the walls with their fine-tipped spears.<br /> Relation from Center - Above<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Autumn Fields<br /> Abode of the Blessed, Watchtower of the Garnet Apple<br /> <b>Koraie:</b> the Witches on the Path of Tears<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Spirit<br /> Among the rolling hills, covered in dried stalks of corn, red, gold and yellow leaves fall perpetually from the sky, despite the lack of trees. Here, the Great Lady of Life &amp; Death waits with her chosen few; souls which have achieved perfect balance with what they were and what they are. They stay here to help other souls pass through into what lays beyond, crying because they will miss those souls, but happy that they are going.<br /> Relation from Center - Over<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Crystal Caves<br /> Abode of Ghouls, Watchtower of the Quartz Spyglass<br /> <b>Asteri:</b> the Stargazers on the Path of Oblivion<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Mind<br /> Under Stygia lies the Timeless Ocean, but Stygia lies beneath all, concealed beneath rock. Within the rock, there are caves containing all manner of worldly riches. Within one cave lies a Watchtower which has tunneled through to the surface. Imbedded within the cave walls are crystals of all colors, glowing faintly, and within this cave, the ghouls wait. They wait for Oblivion. They look to the skies and stars for signs of death and destruction from above. Until that day, they greet those who enter this Kingdom with begging and pleading for answers, signs, and death.<br /> Relation from Center - Up<br /> <br /> Kingdom of the Timeless Ocean<br /> Abode of the Protogenoi, Watchtower of the Coral Goblet<br /> <b>Khresmoi:</b> the Soothsayers on the Path of Inevitability<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Matter<br /> Beneath the surface of Stygia lies the Timeless Ocean, the primordial depths beneath the waves where all things began and must eventually return. Within its depths is the stillness of eternity, the timeless pull of currents that were here before everything and will be here after we are dust. The sea breaks everything down; wears everything away, until nothing is left but the water. Floating with the currents of the sunless sea are the Protogenoi, beings formed when the world first began. They represent the most fundamental aspects of the world: life &amp; death, light &amp; dark, creation &amp; the void, earth &amp; sky. They alone resist the water\u2019s inevitable force, for now. They, too, will break down in the fullness of time. When the world has grown cold and dark, they will fall to pieces, too, and the cycle will begin again. Those who follow the Path of Inevitability come to know just how small and how fleeting they are, and have the utmost respect for the forces which spin the universe along.<br /> Relation from Center - Below </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-03-2014, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T10:33:32-08:00","id":41819,"title":"","content":"Other links regarding nonstandard Watchtowers, as I find them:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default2057-6.html?g=posts&amp;t=66854\" target=\"_blank\">How to build a Watchtower</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd45d-8.html?g=posts&amp;t=36881\" target=\"_blank\">New Paths</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default5d0a-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=35341\" target=\"_blank\">Back-tracing the Pentacle</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2014, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T11:07:18-08:00","id":41831,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver, for the Watchtowers you made, what would you say are the main occult correspondences, attracted personalities and associated philosophies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T11:45:50-08:00","id":41853,"title":"","content":"Please clarify your question by giving an example from one of the official Watchtowers. In particular, I\u2019d like clarification on what you mean by \u201coccult correspondences\u201d.<br /> <br /> The associated philosophies are implied by the \u201cPath of\u2026\u201d names:<br /> \u2022 The Path of Mastery wants to be in control: if you don\u2019t take control of your own life, someone else will. <br /> \u2022 The Path of Excellence wants to find flaws and correct them, and to take what works and make it better.<br /> \u2022 The Path of Balance wants to curb excesses: a time for everything, but everything in moderation.<br /> \u2022 The Path of Discovery wants to solve mysteries. They\u2019re explorers, and the future is an undiscovered country.<br /> \u2022 The Path of Enlightenment wants to educate themselves and others: those who don\u2019t learn from history are doomed to repeat it.<br /> <br /> Mind you, these are stereotypes and gross simplifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-07-2014, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T13:46:09-08:00","id":41939,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Well, with occult correspondences I meant how the Path of Scouring relates to Christian Hell and Purgatory and Asian Demon Kings, Ecstasy is all about the shamanism and so on. Now, most of these are already implied (like Mastery relating to Middle Eastern stories of jinn), but I was curious if you would add some.<br /> <br /> Thanks again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T16:36:52-08:00","id":42030,"title":"","content":"I see. All of the occult correspondences are already implied by the names:<br /> <br /> \u2022 As you say, sorcerers on the Path of Mastery riff off of Arabian Nights and its Djinn.<br /> \u2022 Alchemists on the Path of Excellence riff off of the alchemical Magnum Opus \u2014 turning lead to gold, literally or metaphorically.<br /> \u2022 Druids on the Path of Balance don\u2019t riff off of any authentic mystical beliefs, per se; they\u2019re more attuned to the modern environmentalist movement and its notion that we are caretakers of the Earth. Where the Thyrsus represent a Darwinian struggle for survival and supremacy, the Palinoros are more like shepherds and gardeners.<br /> \u2022 Astrologers on the Path of Discovery invoke stargazing and the principle of As Above, So Below. If you\u2019re familiar with <b>Exalted</b>, the C\u00e6lum should be reminiscent of the Sidereal Exalted: not only do they read peoples\u2019 fortunes in the stars, but they also petition the Stars to <i>shape</i> peoples\u2019 destinies.<br /> \u2022 Bards on the Path of Enlightenment draw from the celtic and norse traditions of bards and skalds, where the bard\u2019s task is to serve as society\u2019s memory. Traditionally, this was done through poems and music, as that made the records easier to recall; as a result, this Path tends to have an association with music and storytelling as magic, and more generally with entertainment and social gatherings as magic.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that these are archetypes emblematic of what the Path is supposed to be about, not straitjackets restricting you to just these concepts, just as being Obrimos doesn\u2019t mean that you\u2019re a holy man or that being a Moros means that you must be a necromancer. Note that the New Legacies for the Path of Enlightenment is deliberately patterned after <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>\u2019s Cult of Ecstasy. That\u2019s because those mages are <i>also</i> seekers of Enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2014, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:01:46-08:00","id":44338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41654#post41654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The five Abyssal Ziggurats, anti-Watchtowers set in Abyssal worlds that resemble elementally-flipped perversions of the Path Realms, that mid-ranking Scelesti journey to. For example, the Anti-Aether is the flooded ocean-floor wreckage of the Nephilim's cities - the cold, dark symbolism of power utterly destroyed as the mirror to the Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds quite interesting, where can I read about these ziggurats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:08:47-08:00","id":44350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=44338#post44338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds quite interesting, where can I read about these ziggurats?</div> </div> </div> </div> Tome of the Mysteries is where it was first printed (last section of the book), but it was reprinted and more fully fleshed out in Left-Hand Path p66.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:57:06-08:00","id":44459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=44350#post44350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tome of the Mysteries is where it was first printed (last section of the book), but it was reprinted and more fully fleshed out in Left-Hand Path p66.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:58:03-08:00","id":44460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41690#post41690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">G\u00e6ans\u201d is a vague term for its denizens, and I was never really happy with it. At various points, I considered serpents, Ent-like tree-people, and Dryads as candidates; but I never settled on a single, consistent set of imagery for the inhabitants of the Kingdom of Seasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said back when you first posted these Watchtowers. I consider Serpents to be perfect. Their shedding skin is metaphorically connected to changing seasons. They're already strongly tied to druids. And Serpents are occasionally part of the planet; in that a landmass is occasionally named a sleeping dragon or suchlike. (Though I can't promise I'm not mixing myth with a myth-inspired fiction book I read)<br /> <br /> You know I actually vastly prefer <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Palinoros</span> to the Thyrus. The Thyrus are the path of a darwinian eat or be eaten world. Both the Primal Wild and the Hisil reflect this. To me, that's what the Exarchs want you to think.<br /> <br /> While in the Primal Wild everything struggles not to be eaten; the Palinoros see a world where death is just the beginning of more life, not a struggle but a gift. The antelope gives it's life to the lion as a gift, the lion gives his life to the grass, which gives it to the antelope (well Mufussa would like it; he's a lion).<br /> <br /> To me it just feels right that the idea of eat or be eaten is a Lie the Exarchs told the world, and the Awakened would see through it and be willing to gladly give their lives as gifts to the next generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-07-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:27:22-08:00","id":48232,"title":"","content":"First of all, thank you very much, Dataweaver, for your image of &quot;The Supernal World as seen by the Awakened&quot;. It's awesome. I'm using it with my group of Mage and we all appreciate it very much. Also, thank you for all the rest of the links <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41718#post41718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mage landed in a particularly magical part of the Primal Wild and got Life/Prime ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of my goals in our chronicle; creating a Life/Prime Watchtower. Has someone done it? Any thought on it?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:21:24-08:00","id":48392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=48232#post48232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of my goals in our chronicle; creating a Life/Prime Watchtower. Has someone done it? Any thought on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my earlier post, my take on Prime/Life combo:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Kingdom of World Trees</b></span><br /> Abode of Dryads, Watchtower of the Oaken Sickle<br /> <b>Verbenae:</b> the Druids on the Path of Sacrifice<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Spirit<br /> With great trees stretching down into the mist and high into the clouds, the Kingdom of World Trees awaits those who would choose Sacrifice as the way to the heavens. Those who visit here will find themselves leaping among the branches and leaves, risking a fall at every step. The Dryads will not help the would-be mage; in fact, they will ask him for assistance. They will beg for water for their drying leaves, ask for help in removing vines and weeds from their tiny, tree-top gardens. Only those who stop and help, and can keep their balance, will be guided to the branches of a great oak. Through a door carved into the side in the shape of a sickle, they can enter the Watchtower and leave their name in this sacred grove.<br /> Relation to Center - Down<br /> <br /> My general thoughts on this was that the card for Obrimos is &quot;Strength&quot;, and this is one who's decided to focus more on life, so I landed on &quot;Sacrifice&quot; for that. A mage who puts life above all and will die for that cause, because they have no greater strength than their life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-13-2014, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T14:27:46-08:00","id":48477,"title":"","content":"When I devise a Watchtower around a pair of Arcana, I start by comparing the Arcana and asking myself, \u201cwhat do these Arcana have in common?\u201d What theme ties them together? A good way to start (though by no means the only one) is to think of what kinds of conjunctional spells you can do with the Arcana. For the Palinoros, the theme I came up with was the cycle of existence: growth and decay. For Life and Prime, my inclination would be to use a mystical \u201clifeforce\u201d as the common thread.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019ve got a tentative theme in hand, I try to find what saibot called an occult correspondence: some archetypal practitioner of magic that resonates with that theme. This, I think is the harder part, especially asmore and more archetypes are claimed by other Watchtowers. Were I adding a Life/Prime Watchtower to the above set, for example, I wouldn\u2019t use druids because they\u2019re already claimed by the Palinoros. If you\u2019re <i>not</i> aiming to have this Watchtower coexist with the Palinoros (as with Papa Bear\u2019s schema), then I\u2019d certainly consider an interpretation of druids as my inspiration.<br /> <br /> After that, it\u2019s a matter of taking the summary text block from <b>Mage</b> and filling in the blanks:<br /> <br /> [Path name], [mystical archetype] on the Path of [one-word summary of theme]<br /> Scions of the Watchtower of [Watchtower name] in the Realm of [Realm name], Kingdom of [different one-word summary of theme] and Abode of [signature creature].<br /> <br /> The first one-word summary of theme should be indicative of the typical attitude and/or goals of someone on this Path; the second one-word summary of theme should reflect something about the world as seen through Path-colored glasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T18:47:53-08:00","id":48639,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, Papa Bear and Dataweaver. Though i'd never would have thougth on Dryads as the epithome of Life/Prime (i would have chosen them as more Fate/Life, maybe, or even Life/Spirit) i actually like your presentation. I would have though, like Dataweaver, of a &quot;Lifeforce&quot;, but the idea of Sacrifice is so appealing... i'll have to consider merging them both. Somehow. I'll give it a serious though and i'll let you know my take on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:23:12-08:00","id":49821,"title":"","content":"I didn't really work it from the angle of Dryads as the Life/Prime type creature. Once I locked in on the World Trees idea, I went to Dryads as a natural fit for a place full of trees. The trees fit better with the sacrifice idea since they are the plant people have used for warmth and shelter for a very long time. They fall so we can rise. Trees are also very important in the Druid system and very connected to their ideas of life and a &quot;lifeforce&quot;. They could just as easily have been Ghillie Dhu or Elves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-15-2014, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:07:41-08:00","id":50251,"title":"","content":"As a side, I think Death &amp; Fate have a lot of themes bringing them together. Perhaps that realm is called...<br /> <br /> <b>Duat</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T20:29:08-08:00","id":50380,"title":"","content":"Due to the Arcadia mess, I tend to shy away from using names for Supernal Realms that are in use by other gamelines for \u201cotherworlds\u201d; but if your intent is to introduce a similar degree of ambiguity (e.g., by implying that the Judges of the Arisen might be residing somewhere in the Supernal World), then by all means introduce a \u201cRealm of Duat\u201d. <br /> <br /> I also tend to shy away from dual-Subtle or dual-Gross Ruling Arcana; but I have less of an aversion to them than I do to conflated naming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T07:57:35-08:00","id":50691,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with DW on recycling names of other worlds and doubling up on the Subtle or Gross Arcana. The names thing is not so much an issue of confusion for me, but more for the thematic problem. Just because there's a vague similarity doesn't mean it should be called the same or something similar. Arcadia got used twice because of the faerie connection. It's the iconic name. Other realms usually have enough different names (Hell, Pandemonium, Hades) they can be switched up.<br /> <br /> As far as the double Subtle or Gross Arcana, it just seems a bit unbalanced. Not in the rules sense, but in the Supernal sense. There has to be a high and a low, not just two highs or two lows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:01:49-08:00","id":50794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b><br /> \u201cG\u00e6ans\u201d is a vague term for its denizens, and I was never really happy with it. At various points, I considered serpents, Ent-like tree-people, and Dryads as candidates; but I never settled on a single, consistent set of imagery for the inhabitants of the Kingdom of Seasons. </div> </div> </div>Is there a reason you rejected Nymphs? The living spirits of biomes seems like a perfect fit to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Path of Excellence wants to find flaws and correct them, and to take what works and make it better. </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the Moros's gig, although that can be an uneasy fit with necromancy, except in specific takes on the latter. Which is to say, I don't think it's too much duplication, but I think you should add something too, namely the imagery of divine/heroic smiths and craftsmen. The Moros deal strip away the chaff to reveal the glorious core - this includes the gold at the heart of matter, and the immortality at the heart of death. The Chrysopos build things up - instead of chaff to be cut away, you have elements to be combined - the glory is the whole, not the core.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T01:10:45-08:00","id":51465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=50794#post50794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason you rejected Nymphs? The living spirits of biomes seems like a perfect fit to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Summoners</b> and its Supernal summons, for one thing. Nymphs are a bit too one-sided: they make some sense when a Palinoros uses Life to summon her Watchtower Realm\u2019s denizens, but not so much sense when using Death. Serpents work better in this regard. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=50794#post50794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of the Moros's gig, although that can be an uneasy fit with necromancy, except in specific takes on the latter. Which is to say, I don't think it's too much duplication, but I think you should add something too, namely the imagery of divine/heroic smiths and craftsmen. The Moros deal strip away the chaff to reveal the glorious core - this includes the gold at the heart of matter, and the immortality at the heart of death. The Chrysopos build things up - instead of chaff to be cut away, you have elements to be combined - the glory is the whole, not the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T06:34:58-08:00","id":51579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=50691#post50691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm with DW on recycling names of other worlds and doubling up on the Subtle or Gross Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree with him, too! I was merely positing another idea because I know there are people here and elsewhere that like trying to fit all the games into the greater nWoD cosmology. In my Mummy game, Duat is its own thing; there's a little bit of crossover that we haven't gotten to yet which might raise questions, but in my personal canon Duat is its own place unrelated to the Supernal, the Underworld, or the Lower Depths (well, maybe it's related to the Depths).<br /> <br /> As for the subtle/gross dichotomy, chalk it up to my unfamiliarity with Mage mechanics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T07:05:50-08:00","id":51595,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, there\u2019s no distinction. Conceptually, Death, Fate Mind, Prime, and Spirit are Subtle, while Forces, Life, Matter, Space, and Time are Gross. (personally, I\u2019d reverse Mind and Space in this regard; sympathetic links and symbolic correspondences feel far more Subtle than brain waves, neural activity, and memory storage systems; but that\u2019s just me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T08:38:06-08:00","id":51636,"title":"","content":"Data, Mind isn't about &quot;neural activity&quot;. This is Life. Mind is about the subjective/cultural side on &quot;emotions, memory, belief, language&quot;<br /> <br /> Space is a bit confusing for me because, all the gross arcana are about &quot;laws of physics&quot; while the subtle are more like &quot;the arcana of the subjective and supernatural&quot;. Space fits both, with its metric-connotation and its sympethy connotation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T16:27:35-08:00","id":51963,"title":"","content":"I respectfully disagree; but I\u2019ll address it in a separate topic to avoid derailing this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T18:20:47-08:00","id":52030,"title":"","content":"I'd say that when it comes to mental processes, there's some Life/Mind overlap; Life affects the grey matter itself, while Mind is more about the energetic contents thereof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:20:39-07:00","id":142371,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is the most appropriate topic but is that entities &quot;living&quot; in a Supernal Realm, depend on the theme of their realm or their arcanum ?<br /> <br /> For example : In a Supernal Realm of Life and Prime* (representing the Garden of Eden, the Golden Age in Greco-Roman mythology and other myths of an original,wild and good condition of the Humanity,ect...);<br /> <br /> the Realm is populated with pacifists Beasts and Cherubs guarding the place or it must be another entities specifics to the Realm ? I do not really have an idea exept Beasts or Cherubs. (and this a citation of the Bible; no more bad than another but maybe they are a more original creature in a mythology ? like Persan or babylonian ? both have ofen similar concepts with judeo-christianism)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Any idea for a name ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:36:09-07:00","id":142418,"title":"","content":"Just call it Eden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:42:19-07:00","id":142423,"title":"","content":"Well, there's really no reason <i>not </i>to just call it &quot;Eden&quot;, and according to a little Google-fu, it had a bunch of guardian Cherubs, so there's really no reason not to use that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T10:41:05-07:00","id":142467,"title":"","content":"I would have liked a little less abrahamic/western-centrist name but I suppose this is not worse than Pandemonium, Stygia or Arcadia,<br /> <br /> Life and Prime are a good choice for the symbolic ? (I thought &quot;Life&quot; for the physical, living and natural side; and &quot;Prime&quot; for the divine, &quot;paradise&quot; side, and the Angels Guards) i don't get a better association<br /> <br /> If you have a idea for the Motivation (Primordial ?), Nimbus, Tarot and Dur-Abzu (I had tought of N\u00f4d but for &quot;forbidden knowledge&quot; they are already anti-aether...)<br /> <br /> The hardest to write a new path, i'ts not avoid making a thematic already made \u200b\u200bby a another or just to mix both ? (I have a little trouble to avoid mixing the Aether and Primal Wyld)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T11:41:28-07:00","id":142579,"title":"","content":"Mesopotamia: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Forest\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Forest</a><br /> Possible Hinduism-derived ones: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_groves_of_India\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_groves_of_India</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:51:27-07:00","id":142646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=142467#post142467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hardest to write a new path, i'ts not avoid making a thematic already made \u200b\u200bby a another or just to mix both ? (I have a little trouble to avoid mixing the Aether and Primal Wyld)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, just look at what Dataweaver and myself have done, you'll see that you're going to step on some thematic toes no matter what. The big thing for me was finding the different spin on each that made it just a little different from the others. But there are often running themes thru either the common Realm (all the ones from Stygia, for example) or the common Arcanum (all the Prime + something else Watchtowers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:50:37-07:00","id":546033,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">S E I D O S</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Monks on the Flowing Path<br /> Scions of the Watchtower of the Silver Spiral in the Realm of Okeanos<br /> Kingdom of Reflection, Abode of the Leviathan</span><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Time, Mind<br /> <b>Supplementary Arcana:</b> Matter<br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum:</b> Prime<br /> <br /> Okeanos is the primordial ocean, whence all waters flow. The passage of time and memory reign supreme here where impermanence, transience and non-attachment are the prevailing themes. Like Arcadia, the supernal realm changes day-to-day with one exception: The Watchtower at its heart. The Watchtower of the Silver Spiral is an enormous, twisting column of water. The crushing power of its tides extends far below even the darkest depths of the ocean to places so remote and inaccessible, none are known to have explored it. Likewise, the Watchtower twists high into the sky, so high that its peak has never been found or even seen. The roaring sound of its severe might is spiritually overwhelming, it is this sound that resounds across the abyss like thunder, calling to the souls of humankind.<br /> <br /> Monks know well that all causal and conditional things are impermanent, lacking any kind of static reality. This direct experience of the inherent instability of reality guides the Seidos Mages. They seldom put down roots, form lasting relationships or stay in one place for very long. With the ability to look backwards through time and to clarify the mind, they can reconcile memories with actual events and this clarity of the past would make them ideal historians if only they believed in recording history. Likewise, they are able to look forward into the future and plan for it in great detail, commanding their minds to take note of what\u2019s important and to ignore what isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Their supplementary Arcanum, Matter, relates to the literal aquatic quality of the Supernal Realm they\u2019ve awakened to. Seidos Mages find it much easier to manipulate fluids than any other kind of matter and, especially, liquid water.<br /> <br /> Although not necessarily related to their Awakening, many monks seem to be physically strong. Perhaps the crushing power of the churning ocean inspires Seidos Mages to engage in strength training. Regardless of the reason, it is a curious trend among the Monks as noted by the Silver Ladder and Mysterium who do keep track of these kinds of things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:13:48-07:00","id":546567,"title":"","content":"It might entirely be just me, but when coming to new paths, I prefer to consider the archetype first- all the paths have clear archetypes like warlock, necromancer, or shaman.<br /> <br /> The new supernal &quot;realms&quot; are nice and all, but in first edition in which mages maybe spent a whole 5 minutes in their entire lives it just seems like putting the cart in front of the horse to do it the &quot;okay, here's this new realm, what kind of mage would draw power from it?&quot; <br /> <br /> Of course now that in second edition the supernal is basically the back stage of reality that mages have a lifelong pass to, they're both important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:22:01-07:00","id":546572,"title":"","content":"What's important in 2e, even more than the Archetype(s), is the way the Path's Ruling Arcana appear to Mage Sight, followed closely by what kind of Supernal entities your Path deals with. Granted, these are intimately connected to the Archetypes\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T00:38:43-07:00","id":549862,"title":"","content":"I agree that the biggest concern is the archetype of 'mage/wizard/witch' that would be drawn from the realm. I have my own list of realms and I went with &quot;Arabic-Djinn Contract Binder Magic&quot; &quot;Japanese Oni-Baba/Shinto Priest dichotomy&quot; &quot;Maori Wind-Caller&quot; &quot;Judao Mystic Number Reader&quot; and &quot;Aztec/Incan Blood-letter&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a lot of room to expand those idea in my opinion. Our players seem more interested in WHAT they do then WHERE the come from. So the next step for me was Mage Sight symbolism and Supernal Entities like Jaguar-Men that hunted down the end of time. All this work for another ST that ran with the ideas. I don't have permission yet to post them here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T19:57:49-08:00","id":834204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41654#post41654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one Supernal World, seen through five different interpretations.<br /> <br /> That said, Left Hand Path has both of the hinted at alternatives in it.<br /> <br /> A Tremere legend of a sixth Watchtower of the Soul that would encompass all the existing Paths and is either a) a delusion b) a warped interpretation of a Lower Depth c) in the abyss or d) related to a Bound - that is, it was in the Supernal, but has been removed.<br /> <br /> The five Abyssal Ziggurats, anti-Watchtowers set in Abyssal worlds that resemble elementally-flipped perversions of the Path Realms, that mid-ranking Scelesti journey to. For example, the Anti-Aether is the flooded ocean-floor wreckage of the Nephilim's cities - the cold, dark symbolism of power utterly destroyed as the mirror to the Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div> what's the other anti-realms like? i dont have a cop of Left Hand path with me ;/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:25:30-07:00","id":944858,"title":"","content":"So first off, apologies for this thread necromancy. I'm finally (and temporarily) crawling out from under the rock of dissertation proposal writing. Enough so that I can finally finish reading Mage 2nd ed and post some 10 (or 11) Path/Watchtower hacks that I've been sitting on for months. Remembering all of the controversy about the rules when 2nd ed was first released, I will say that after reading through the book I've personally found the rules as sound as those produced by the other 2nd editions (which is to say a step above those for Demon and Beast -- but to be fair Demon and Beast didn't have over a decade of playing to inform the shape of their mechanics so...and really the mechanics of those games are solid--they just have some rough edges). <br /> <br /> The primary reason for these alternative Path hacks is to create a more heterogeneous Supernal with more Paths and more player options. One of the things I've chosen to do is to separate Gross magicians from Subtle magicians. This is partially because I find the choices of minor arcanum to be a bit arbitrary (but that is the effects of choosing 'good for the story' over 'logical consistency').<br /> <br /> Since to some extent the Mage ecosystem is a reflection of academia, I wanted to better highlight how heterogeneous yet systematic differences between Paths would be in a rendition that resembles the academic milieu even more closely. This take on the Paths varies greatly from what's presented in the 2nd ed. book, so don't expect a minor change vis-a-vis Paths. I also wanted to play around with the symbolism of the Awakened Tarot (recall that there are 22 major arcana in the tarot deck) to a much greater extent than the main 2nd ed book does. Hopefully we'll see some hacks similar to these in upcoming Storyteller focused books.<br /> <br /> Without further ado:<br /> <b>Gross Paths:<br /> </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Alphaios: Ascetics &amp; Gurus on the Path of Scourging</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Alphaios employ Life and Time to achieve mastery over themselves. In human tales and legends they appear as wild hermits and lonely figures dwelling far beyond civilization. When they can be engaged in sharing their knowledge with their fellow human beings, we call them Gurus and thank them for their guidance in overcoming our own inner demons, but far more often we call them Ascetics: those who have abandoned society and relationships with others to cultivate their own Inner Being.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You think you've seen them but they often take forms you hadn't considered.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The kindly old man down the street offers you a bit of advice in passing. You've heard the tales that he was once married but his wife died young. He once had children but they died too. He's a miserly fellow that pays no attention to the community. He just dwells in his ramshackle old house and keeps his neighbors at arm's length. But if these things are all true why is he telling you that dietary changes will help you overcome your night terrors? How does he know that you suffer them at all?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Everyone thinks the local crazy lady is homeless but one day you and your friends got lost hiking in the woods. As you hopelessly weaved to and fro, unable to find your way back, you caught sight of her. Her simple stare from behind a far off tree seemed disappointed. She was long gone by the time you reached that tree, but you caught sight of her again and again until she delivered you back to familiar places.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">That's what Ascetics do: pave the path to better living by example.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Alphaios Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Time</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: They're the Inanitan powers that govern physical change. They're the twin motive forces of birth and entropy that make choice possible and scribe out the terrible weight of consequence into the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the wellspring from which agency is born. From it comes the ability to make choices. It governs growth, health, and abundance. But it also brings about largesse, indolence, and disease. It is the power of shaping oneself and those around one. A wise Ascetic knows how to temper herself and those around her into their optimum forms. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Time</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the river that folds and hammers the living into their new forms as they constantly choose and change. It carves experience into their souls and lets growth unfold at the pace it is meant to. It trains the body through cycles of plenty and scarcity. It delivers the consequences of choices onto the choosers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Space</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The endless wastelands of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inanitas</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are a blasted landscape that look the same no matter which direction one faces. They are not to be navigated by choice and quickly punish the living who try. By some supernal design, those who wish to travel the wastes must first still their bodies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols and Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hermit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hanged Man</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Loners, demons, and ascetics. Stories of enlightenment, inner powers, and great temptations. Pain and privation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Awakened Tarot, the Alphaios personifies the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hermit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: an introspective soul constantly seeking to know himself. Ascetics pursue their introspection by denying themselves the pleasures of the world. The live simple lives and employ their magic as a means to bolster their ability to endure adverse conditions around them. Their mysteries involve the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hanged Man</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, a card representing the perpetual need to sacrifice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ascetics are well known for invoking </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Demons</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> who harry, castigate, and tempt them. It is only by constantly testing one\u2019s mettle that one can achieve their perfect form. Many Alphaios bind personal demons to themselves so that they are perpetually challenged on a daily basis, for only by having their decisions cross-examined can they truly understand the consequences that spiral forth from them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">An Alphaios usually employs tarnished, decayed, or worn materials as yantras for her spells. Clay bowls symbolizing the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Empty Bowl</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are a typical ritual tool employed by Ascetics. Staves of dried, twisted wood, tarnished coins, and rods fashioned from sunbleached bones are also commonly seen tools. When the Mages who walk the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Scourging</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are forced to defend themselves they employ barbed clubs, whips, and other cruel weapons that are often coated in rust or stained and tarnished.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Choice &amp; Consequence</li> <li>Major Arcana: Life &amp; Time</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Space</li> <li>Oracle: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">Alphaios</span></li> <li>Watchtower: The Empty Bowl</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Hermit &amp; The Hanged Man</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Daemons &amp; Daimons</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Inanitas</li> <li>Yantras: Tarnished coins, clay bowls, dried wood, sunbleached bones, distressed materials; Barbed clubs, whips, cruel weapons<br /> <br /> Acanthus: Alchemists &amp; Enchanters on the Path of Wonder</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Acanthus wield power over Time and Matter. In legend they frequently appear in the form of apothecaries and smiths. When they can be persuaded to set aside their arcane experiments to craft wonders for their fellow humans, we name them Enchanters and marvel at the marvels they forge. Far more often they cannot be roused from the sanctuary of their laboratories where they pursue knowledge for its own sake and we name them Alchemists. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Acanthus often hide in plain sight much as they have done since bygone ages when they and people like them played important roles central to a community\u2019s health.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The young woman at the pharmacy window hands you your medication and cautions you to use it as instructed. You don\u2019t realize that after work she retires to an abandoned school-house. It\u2019s ramshackle chemistry lab looks like someone has repurposed it to cook meth and other designer drugs. It\u2019s real purpose is hidden in the arcane symbols and otherworldly reagents that she has gathered in her quest for the Philosopher\u2019s Stone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Your teenaged boy retreats to the family basement every night. You think that he\u2019s just playing with the old chemistry set that you gave him one Christmas when he was eight. Your sleeping eyes never apprehend the fact that he\u2019s moved beyond transmuting lead into gold. You never realize that the special tea he keeps brewing for you is the only thing holding the cancer you don\u2019t even know you have at bay.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Acanthus Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Matter</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Time</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Pandemonic forces of creation itself. They are the dualistic forces that weave existence itself from the nothingness of the void. Every Acanthus knows that it isn\u2019t enough to simply create things; true creation requires time to become. The Acanthus approach to magic is the most patient of all Paths and, it is not unusual for their arcane works to take years or even decades to mature into fruition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Matter</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the arcanum that holds dominion over the stuff of creation. Its constituents fashion the basic building blocks from which all things are woven. It represents the firmament upon which all things extend, energy given physical form. A wise Alchemist always seems to know exactly which substance is needed for a given task.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Time</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is carrier through which one substance changes into another substance. It is the process of chemical interaction itself. Its passage blazes the trail by which material substances share their essential essences and participate in the perpetual cycle of bonding and unbonding. It is the experience through which things mature into new forms. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Forces</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The chaotic, ever-changing landscapes of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pandemonium</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are a living history of substances coming together to form new substances before breaking apart to reemerge as their sovereign selves. While heat and cold are by-products of these processes it is the materials forged through the passing ages that define the place and, their greedy interactions with one another subsume the forces around them, leaving little ambient energy for visitors to benefit from.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lovers </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">World</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Alignment, union, integration, and accomplishment. Tales of invention, creation, adulteration, and maturation. Chemical reactions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Awakened Tarot, the Acanthus stands for the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lovers</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: the fundamental relationships among all things. Alchemists\u2019 obsessions are rooted in the unions of the simple materials of the universe which lead to more complex substances which themselves can be bound together. They use their magic to uncover the fundamental truths of all of creation. The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">World</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> lies at the heart of their mysteries, signifying their need for accomplishment and to complete their imperfect understanding of everything around them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Alchemists sometimes summon </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Chimeras</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, amalgamations of mythical and living beasts, to aid them in their arcane science. These creatures provide valuable ingredients such as fur, ichor, spines, and venom that Alchemists employ in their experiments. In turn the Acanthus pay the Chimeras tithes of Mana or favors, which occasionally lead to substantial bonds between the two.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Of all the Awakened, Acanthus are the ones who employ impossible, refined, and volatile materials as components of their spellcraft. Heavy, metal scaled gloves fashioned from steel, orichalcum, mithril, or adamantine symbolize the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and are often employed in the alchemical practices that shape Acanthus\u2019 rituals. Wands and rods of glass, staves of wrought iron, steel coins, granite mortars, and glass beakers are common tools of the Alchemist\u2019s Path and, in times of conflict Mages who walk the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Wonder</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> gird themselves with blades fashioned from star metal and other rare or difficult to manufacture substances. Contemporary weapons that employ the fire of chemistry, such as guns and grenades, are also popular choices in war comes calling. </span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Maturation &amp; Creation</li> <li>Major Arcana: Time &amp; Matter</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Forces</li> <li>Oracle: Acanthus</li> <li>Watchtower: The Iron Gauntlet</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Lovers &amp; The World</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Anachronisms &amp; Apeirons</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Pandemonium</li> <li>Yantras: Iron coins, glass beakers, granite, sulfur, volatile materials; Fire, grenades, weapons forged from impossible materials like adamantine and orichalcum <br /> <br /> Paramonimos: Geomancers &amp; Masons on the Path of Control</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Paramonimos are privy to the secret workings of the Space and Forces arcana. In tales they are often cast in the roles of leaders who are responsible for choosing the locations of new settlements and planning out the layout of those municipal centers. When they play the role of Mason they are typically responsible for the construction great civil works that all share a stake in. Far more often they wear the mantle of Geomancer and are the architects of great arcane designs that weave Sleepers and Awakened alike into the weft of their fabric.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Paramonimos sometimes hide by operating in the open as professionals that work in civil engineering or architecture. They are just as likely to work from the shadows though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You thank the middle-aged woman who handed you the architectural plans for your house\u2019s new addition. Happy with the shape of the new space, you never suspect that she arranged the foundation, walls, and ceiling to provide an invisible sanctuary for you from the myriad things that creep about in the night. All you know is that months later, after the carpenters and contractors have finished building it, you always awaken feeling refreshed and new anytime you have the occasion to fall asleep in it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The aged politician calmly explains to you and everyone else assembled why the street intersection needs to be broadened into a roundabout. You find his explanation for why a grand fountain at the roundabout\u2019s center is necessary to complete the project compelling. You know nothing of the ley lines running below the streets that he hopes to constrain. Nor are you aware that his staff was responsible for arranging the seating and interior decorations for the municipal council\u2019s public hearing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Paramonimos Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Forces</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Space</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Tractian arcana that rule motion. They are the primary colors in which locomotion is painted. By mixing them together a Paramonimos can achieve control over their surroundings by determining where and what kind of force is to be applied.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Forces</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the arcanum that weaves the elemental energies of the world into one vibrant spectrum. The chill of cold, the heat of fire, the lift of air, the crackling sizzle of electricity, and even the impulse transmitted by the impact of solid earth, all of these things can be mastered through knowledge of Forces. And once some modicum of mastery has been achieved, all of these things can be applied to bring about some effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Space</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the infinite canvas upon which reality is etched. While it\u2019s essential nature is timeless, every instant of its existence is tightly bound by the situation that is carved into its many-dimensional form. A knowledgeable Geomancer employs their knowledge of Space to ensure that every application of Forces, be they natural or arcane, is carefully constrained to its proper place.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Time: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The ageless structures and landscapes of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tractus </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">never change. This place forms an endless labyrinth of temples containing whirlwinds that never stop spinning, columns of fire that never cease burning, and bolts of lightning suspended between walls. Whole cities, both those lost to the sands of time and those that have yet to be conceived, stand here. While visitors can find any construct, building, and physical place that they can imagine, nothing new can be fashioned for the abstractness of form itself exists outside of the linear thought processes of living minds.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Emperor</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chariot</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Control, assertion, structure, and foundation. Stories of constraint, the elements, and the application of forces both arcane and natural. Ley lines and configurations.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Awakened Tarot, Paramonimos wear the mantle of the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Emperor</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Geomancers arrange symbols, materials, and structures to control, constrain, and manage the forces that ceaselessly move around them. The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chariot</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> bears the essence of their mysteries, carrying them to the places where control needs to be asserted and marking the extent of their mastery.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">As the Mages whose magic is the most reliant on specific places, Geomancers frequently summon forth </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Genius Loci</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. These beings are often yoked to harvest mana or seal elemental forces into place. Many Geomancers will bind themselves to the beings who represent their sanctums lending them a small amount of substance in exchange for ritual aid, arcane tutelage, and even supernatural defense.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geomancers often employ valuable materials such as jade, silk, vellum, and even hand-crafted paper in the material workings of their spells. Highly detailed, ornate compasses, hand carved from ebony or other precious woods represent the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Ebon Compass</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and play a vital role in a Geomancer\u2019s ritualistic spatial planning. Plates fashioned from jade, staves of lacquered ironwood, and alabaster wands decorated with silk ribbons or lengths of carefully knotted paper are frequently employed as implements by those walking the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Control</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. When Geomancers are forced into physical conflicts that deny them the direct application of elemental energies, they are known to employ chains, chakrams, and other esoteric or improvised weaponry. A cornered Geomancer can be a dangerous opponent because they always seem to know which of the things in their immediate vicinity best lends itself to their defense.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Constraint &amp; Application</li> <li>Major Arcana: Space &amp; Forces</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Time</li> <li>Oracle: Paramonimos</li> <li>Watchtower: The Ebon Compass</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Emperor &amp; The Chariot</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Architektonias &amp; Orismas</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Tractus</li> <li>Yantras: Ebony coins, jade plates, paper, silk, valued materials; Chakrams, chains, esoteric or improvised weapons<br /> <br /> Daidalos: Conjurers &amp; Thaumaturges on the Path of Progress</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>If Acanthus are mad chemists, and Paramonimos are grand architects, then Daidalos are the tinkers among the Awakened. Stories focused on them often tell the tales of the creation of things that were better left uncreated. When they affect objects from afar we know them as Thaumaturges. Typically Daidalos are far more renowned for their skills as Conjurers, bringing ordinarily impossible things into existence by exploiting the secrets encoded within the hidden essence of the Matter and Space arcana.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Daidalos maintain hidden, sometimes hermetic, existences. The world\u2019s Sleepers almost never realize that they\u2019ve encountered one until they are confronted by things that are clearly impossible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You\u2019ve always felt pity for the homeless man who dwells in the junkyard two blocks over. It\u2019s clear from all of the steel sculptures he makes that he\u2019s some kind of savant. You would have never guessed that each of his creations possesses some unnatural spark of life, even though you get the strange sense that they\u2019re watching you as you run by the yard every day during your morning jog. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Everyone is amazed by the skill and luck of the cat burglar who has become the scourge of the region. You\u2019d all be even more amazed if you saw her in action and witnessed how she seems to have a tool for everything. No matter what the contingency, there always seems to be something in her pockets for overcoming it. Even the fluffy white rabbits she leaves as her calling card are produced from spaces no one imagines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Daidalos Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Matter</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Space</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Voluntian opposites that form the essential building blocks for the Fallen World. They are both presence and absence, existence and nothingness, two faces of the same coin. The caricature of life. The proceeds of artifice. Daidalos learn their secrets to refine the world around them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Matter</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> provides Conjurers with the grist they use to mill the world anew. It allows them to realize even their most feverish imaginings in the permanence of raw substance. While they might not craft life itself, any manner of unaging simulacra might be fashioned. Tools and raw materials are always at a Conjurer\u2019s fingertips.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Space</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> symbolizes the absence of substance to Conjurers. They employ its secrets to bring materials, tools, and even people and animals from afar to their side. They can also employ it to send the summoned away again. The greatest among them though, understand that it can be used to fold substance in upon itself to create objects that are bigger on the inside than the outside.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Life: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The lands and seas of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Voluntus</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are seemingly full of creatures of all manners and descriptions. Vast cities and sprawling factories dot its surface. But nothing living moves in any of those places. Those making the pilgrimage to source of Conjurers\u2019 power find a strange realm filled with clockwork animals, clay people, and stranger facsimiles of the living.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Justice</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Devil</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Truth, law, the unnatural order of things, permanence. Materialism, artifice, transgressions, forbidden acts of creation. Simulacra and facsimiles.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Daidalos act as the hands of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Justice</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> in the Awakened Tarot. It is only through their familiarity with the Fallen World\u2019s supernatural laws that they are able to work around them, bend them, break them, and occasionally, ignore them altogether. Daidalos mysteries are symbolized through the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Devil</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Every Conjurer must make some amount of peace with their ingrained desire to push the envelope of what can be done with their arcane mastery over substance and its absence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Daidalos frequently dabble in the creation of artificial life. More than a few of their number have been known to summon </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Golems</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to aid them in their explorations. Especially skilled or foolishly curious Conjurers have even been known to persuade such entities into agreements through which their raw essence is reforged into supernatural clockwork automatons, or other even more unusual artificial beings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Conjurers employ hand-crafted implements, mass-produced substances, and other products of human artifice in the spellworks. Small jeweler\u2019s hammers carefully crafted from pure aluminum are indispensable ritual tools representing the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Watchtower of the Aluminum Hammer</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Concrete troughs, aluminum rods, wands hewn from granite, and rune-etched oak staves are common accoutrements employed by those whose feet are on the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Progress</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. When Conjurers are confronted by conflict the prefer to employ mechanical weapons like crossbows, or more recently compound bows, and any weapon that resembles or can be employed as a tool, such as picks, hammers, and similar objects.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Permanence &amp; Transgression</li> <li>Major Arcana: Matter &amp; Space</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Life</li> <li>Oracle: Daidalos</li> <li>Watchtower: The Aluminum Hammer</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: Justice &amp; The Devil</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Idealisms &amp; Myths</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Voluntus</li> <li>Yantras: Aluminum coins, concrete troughs, carved wood, hewn stone, worked materials; Crossbows, picks, tool-like weapons<br /> <br /> Mastigos: Warlocks &amp; Wizards on the Path of Thorns</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Mastigos are the stereotypical magicians that appear in traditional high fantasy stories. They wield the elemental forces of the world as though they were living things. In stories that cast them as supporting characters who aid the main characters with their wisdom and knowledge they are called Wizards. More popularly they are cast in the roles of villain or anti-hero and we know them by the name, Warlock.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Even when they make their homes in bustling cities, Mastigos often dwell apart from the world. When they bother with employment they tend to hold jobs that permit them to cultivate their interests from the relative safety of plain sight.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The woman from the forestry service was nice enough to let you and your boyfriend off with a warning. You knew that the forest preserve was closed at that hour of the night which was why you chose to park there. You\u2019ll never realize the real reason that she chased you away is that the invisible, arcane energies born from your lust interfered with her own after-hours rituals.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Everyone agrees that the philosophy lecturer at the junior college is an odd bird. He\u2019s late to his own lectures, seems to daydream during office hours, and spends more time wandering around the campus than in the building outside of those specific times. You don\u2019t understand that he\u2019s constantly marveling at the world around him. The perpetual information overload allows him to see how the world is alive in ways that you could never perceive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mastigos Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Forces</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Arcadian principles of energy that align and link all things. The results of fear, anxiety, and illusion released unto the world. The vitality, positivity, and success that results from confrontation. The exposure of all that is hidden.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Forces</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> provide Warlocks with the means to release the world around them from Abyss-induced Sleep that confines it. Mastery of its elemental secrets provides its practitioners with the strange and violent abilities popularized by genre literature and fantasy culture. It is the illusion of strength.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The secrets of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> hold the means for Warlocks to confront the world around them. Without the energy of the living, existence can have no meaning and the knowledge hidden in all things cannot be revealed. It is the font of warmth that comes from understanding one\u2019s connections among the web of all things. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Matter</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Arcadia</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is a supernal realm that seethes and roils with life. Each and every thing, no matter how base of an element is its own vital entity. From the wind, lightning, and rain, to the most sullen and stagnant puddle, nothing is inert. Mages whose spellcraft calls for raw materials find that there is a dearth of such things there for even Arcadia\u2019s seas and deserts breathe and move. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moon</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sun</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Illusion, fear, and anxiety. Success, positivity, and vitality. Confrontation and release. Overcoming obstacles.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mastigos symbolize the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moon</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> in the Awakened Tarot. Their world-altering arcane powers inspire insecurity in others which suits these Warlocks fine for they have long realized that only by confronting one\u2019s insecurities directly can one hope to dispel life\u2019s illusions and arrive at a more fully actualized self. Their mysteries involve the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sun</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Possessing and wielding power isn\u2019t an end in and of itself. Release from the prison of one\u2019s own illusions can only come about through the proper application of power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Elementals</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are often summoned by Warlocks as a means to further their goals of Awakening those around them or Ascending beyond themselves. Particularly powerful Warlocks will bind such entities to their service in order to accumulate even more power over their surroundings. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Warlocks fit long established fantasy tropes by employing polished metal, still water, crystals, and other reflective materials in their spells. They frequently embroider their clothing or other cloth based sanctum objects with a single silver long-stemmed rose to symbolize their deep connection to the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Particularly skilled Warlocks sometimes cultivate actual, unnatural silver roses. Spotless porcelain mortars, brilliant silver coins, hardwood staves polished to a reflective gleam, and wands tipped with crystals or gems are frequently employed spell-casting implements for those who walk the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Thorns</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Warlocks employ long knives, swords with curved blades, and other practical weapons (even well-maintained handguns and rifles) when they march to battle. </span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Release &amp; Confrontation</li> <li>Major Arcana: Forces &amp; Life</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Matter</li> <li>Oracle: Mastigos</li> <li>Watchtower: The Lunargent Thorn</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Moon &amp; The Sun</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Elementals &amp; Imps</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Arcadia</li> <li>Yantras: Silver coins, porcelain mortars, polished hardwood, crystal, reflective materials; Curved swords, long knives, practical weapons</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:27:24-07:00","id":944859,"title":"","content":"Apparently in 2 parts...<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle Paths:<br /> </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moros: Necromancers &amp; Sages on the Path of Loss</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Moros tread a path that reveals truths lost to the entropic forces of the past. They explore arcane forces that normal mortals dread: the crucible of change--Death, and the echo of meaning--the Mind. Fables that ascribe beneficial roles of advising people how best to cope with loss name them Sages. In darker fairy tales they are more commonly described as performing all manners of unsavory congress with the dead and so name them Necromancers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Among the the denizens of the Fallen World, Necromancers make themselves easily overlooked by cleaving close to the objects of their arcane study. They typically find positions that will regularly bring them into contact with the dead and the dying.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You thanked the pathologist who calmly told you that your brother\u2019s unexpected death was quick and painless. You never discover that she merely confirmed the cause of the death by sawing his skull open and, that word of its quickness and painlessness came from the lips of your brother\u2019s ghost. In truth, she learns as much from the deceased themselves as she does from their inert bodies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You had hit rock bottom when the young priest visited you in the hospital. You never knew that it was your late great grandmother\u2019s ghost that brought him to you. But you were thankful that your talk revived your memories of her. If she survived Nazi death camps, then surely you can survive your crucible too. The memories the conversation brings forth helps steel your will and by the time he leaves you know you\u2019ll persevere.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moros Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Death </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mind</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Stygian doorways to other-wheres and other-whens. From them unfurl manifold resting places for secrets both unknown and forgotten. They are the pathways, both brilliant and shadowed, that lead to every place ever imagined.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the primordial force of entropy. All too often cast as the reducer and destroyer of all things, Necromancers realize its true nature is that of transitional force. There is an impermanence to all things. Even apparently immortal beings have realized their own ever-changing nature, saying, \u201cTransient beings are we.\u201d Death is the principal force of change for whole beings, entire systems, complete communities, and similar entities of scale.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mind</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the solitary fortress of memory. And even when a newborn butterfly emerges from its chrysalis, it is Mind that recalls that it was once a catepillar. Necromancers plumb its depths to learn secrets kept only by the legion of dead. It allows things long forgotten to be found and known, if imperfectly, through the lens of imagination. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Spirit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stygia </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">is drab grey wasteland where only the dead dwell. As such the spirits of the living have no power and Mages whose spellcraft relies on them find their powers drastically constrained. So inimical is this supernal realm that spirits who accidently wander into its endless ashen plains or find themselves upon the cold black waters of the Styx quickly fade away or slowly turn into unliving ghosts of themselves.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Judgement</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Transition, change, and transformation. Absolution, reincarnation, and rebirth. Memories, both remembered and lost.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Unsurprisingly, Moros are synonymous with </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> in the Awakened Tarot. They deal with ghosts, the unliving, and other entities that have transitioned from one state to another. Their mysteries are centered around </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Judgement </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">which delivers the new beginnings promised by every ending. For Necromancers, every change comes layered in hidden meanings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When the ghosts of the Fallen World are no longer able to answer their questions then many Necromancers will turn to </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Shades</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, shadows of memories long forgotten, for inspiration and counsel. The greatest Necromancers will sometimes bind such entities to their will so that knowledge of the past is ever at their beck and call.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Necromancers employ materials that were previously entombed within the earth for their magical practices. Every Moros bears with her a lead coin that represents </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Lead Coin</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Those who walk the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Loss</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> frequently use pewter chalices, wands or rods fashioned from old bones and gemstones soldered into rings or medallions as aids in their rituals. When conflict arises they prefer to arm themselves with hammers, maces, and other blunt weaponry that is capable of crushing bones for it is not unusual for an enraged Necromancer to find occasion to employ the dead themselves as weapons.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Transition &amp; Memories</li> <li>Major Arcana: Death &amp; Mind</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Spirit</li> <li>Oracle: Moros</li> <li>Watchtower: The Lead Coin</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: Death &amp; Judgement</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Shadows &amp; Specters</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Stygia</li> <li>Yantras: Lead coins, pewter chalices, bones, gems, buried materials; Hammers, maces, crushing weapons<br /> <br /> Thyrsus: Mystics &amp; Shamans on the Path of Ecstasy</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Thyrsus tales involve intervening in spiritual matters. When those tales speak of interventions that bolster the boundaries between the world of spirits and that of humans, they speak of the works of Shamans. Many tales speak of interventions that rupture the boundaries written by the fickle hands of the fates. Such tales speak of the works of Mystics. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Divided from the spiritual world by the Gauntlet, most Sleepers have little need for a Mystic\u2019s interventions. The majority of Thyrsus are forgotten by their mortal contemporaries and lead furtive lives in the shadows of decaying cultures.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The stomp dance leader looks like a medicine man. You don\u2019t believe for an instant that he actually has magical powers, no matter what stories your grandmother tells you. You put your trust in modern technologies: pills in bottles, chemical disinfectants, and machine diagnostics. You never realize that those practices all directly derive from older ones he still employs or that they still serve the same purpose of keeping the spiritual in equilibrium with the living.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You look down on the big game hunter. All you can see is the obvious damage he causes to the environment around him. You don\u2019t comprehend the true nature of his intercession. You never see the prey\u2019s acceptance of its fate and you can\u2019t understand the role he plays in helping it transition from one state to the next.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Thyrsus Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Fate</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Lustrian pathways to the future. The inexorable progression towards becoming. The boundaries between what-is and what-is-yet-to-be. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fate</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> weaves the story of existence itself. In its knotted threads every Mystic can see what a thing was and what it will become. It is the immutable boundary between the past and the future which must be pierced in order for things to find their proper places.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">All things contain a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and skillful Mystics can converse with them. In doing so a Mystic can learn the secrets of what is meant to be and recognize violations in the natural order of things. Particularly skilled Mystics can even pierce the boundary between the Fallen World and the Spirit World and interact with the Darwinian entities that live there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Mind: Lustra</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is a purified realm filled with fauna, flora, and fungi of all descriptions. These highly spiritual beings exist in perfect harmony with one another. Predators never consume more prey than necessary, herbivores never overgraze, and vegetation never overgrows. This perfect harmony is only possible because nothing reasons about its place. There are no questions asked and no thoughts had. Everything acts in accord to its primary nature. Mages whose spellcraft relies upon the output of living minds are at a disadvantage for harmonious beings do not distinguish among their bodies, minds, or spirits. All are one. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Empress</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Star</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Boundaries, barriers, and walls. Intercession, action, animus. Fertility, nature, abundance. Spirituality, renewal, inspiration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Awakened Tarot, Thyrsus are signified by the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Empress</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. They are deeply connected to the natural world and the animistic spirits that inhabit the things within it. Their mysteries are closely intertwined with the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Star</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> which guides them on their journey.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mystics often summon </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Beasts</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to their aid. These entities provide valuable insights or can be employed to guide Mystics to places they are needed. Frequently appearing in the guise of animals, many Mystics form special bonds with creatures that they repeatedly summon and interact with.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stone, wood, leather, earth, and other natural materials form the base upon which Mystics build their magical practices. A smooth round stone, sometimes granite or limestone, and sometimes a semi-precious stone like quartz or geodes, is used to symbolize their connection to the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Singing Stone</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Turquoise coins, wooden mugs, and wands, rods, and staves fashioned from wood and decorated with uncut, nature-shaped stones round out the ritual tools employed by those on the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Ecstasy</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. When Mystics find they must employ violence to champion a cause the typically employ axes, javelins, and other weapons used specifically for hunting, like rifles and shotguns.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Boundaries &amp; Intercession</li> <li>Major Arcana: Spirit &amp; Fate</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Mind</li> <li>Oracle: Thyrsus</li> <li>Watchtower: The Singing Stone</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Empress &amp; The Star</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Atavisms &amp; Totems</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Lustra</li> <li>Yantras: Turquoise coins, wooden mugs, leather, hemp, natural materials; Axes, slings, hunting weapons<br /> <br /> Chrysanthos: Psychonauts &amp; Sorcerers on the Path of Might</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Stories of the Chrysanthos involve the universal principles of that are fundamental to all of existence. They are the namers of all things and through naming they spin the fabric of knowledge into being from the nothingness of ignorance. In stories that have them turn their keen perceptions outward, we call them Sorcerers and attribute powers both terrible and malign to them. More typically though, stories showcase them turning their perceptive minds inward, growing cold and indifferent to their fellow human beings as they take up the awesome mantle of Psychonaut.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Psychonauts hide right beneath the noses of the Sleepers around them. They take on appearances that are both familiar and alien to us.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You watch your comatose daughter as she lies still and asleep. You morne all of the things she will never learn about had she the normal life that you\u2019ve had. You remain blissfully unaware of the universe of infinite possibilities that her Awakened mind has just discovered. You never understand that your tears are for the experiences you are missing out on. She lives a silent life that you wouldn\u2019t be able to fathom even if you knew of it. Through your dreams, she gives you brief windows looking out onto the myriad places she has seen, all in the vague hope that they\u2019ll shake you Awake but, you never stir.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You shake your head in pity for the drug addict shooting up in the corner. You believe that he has settled into the corner in order to set himself adrift in a soporific sea of dull sensation. You don\u2019t know that the needle contains a harmless quantity of saline or that he\u2019s just beginning his work day. You are totally ignorant of the inner worlds he has to traverse while he seeks out the deepest held secrets of existence itself. If you had an inkling of what he was truly about, the knowledge might drive you insane.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chrysanthos Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mind</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prime</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Signian forces responsible for conceptualization, action, and actualization. The communicative principles interlinking all things. Arcane mathematics.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mind</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the principal force that empowers Psychonauts. It permits them to make sense of the world around them. Concepts, propositions, language, and meaning all spring forth from its infinite depths. It is the framework through which communication between intelligences becomes possible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prime</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the motive force that enables Psychonauts to realize the products of their minds\u2019 toils. Symbols, systems, utterances, and intentions all descend from its ascendent heights. It is the substance through which communiques propagate outwards, like ripples in water. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Fate:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Among Pychonauts, the mind\u2019s processes and the reality written out through their application are paramount. The Supernal Realm of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Signum</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> realizes the ideal form of these interactions. In it is a place where the will to envision and the will to realize are principal forces. Mages whose spellcraft relies on the happenstance of destiny find their powers are greatly weakened for Signum\u2019s denizens are masters of their own destinies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Mythology</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magician</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Strength</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Power, skill, action. Courage, control, compassion. Command of one\u2019s self and one\u2019s destiny. Perception, conception, the naming of all things.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chrysanthos symbolize the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magician</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> in the Awakened Tarot. Theirs is the power over the very stuff that comprises magic--motive power and the will to use it. While most Psychonauts spend their time obsessing over esoteric things that are far beyond the simple borders of the Fallen World, their mysteries are deeply intertwined with </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Strength</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, which provides them clues regarding when they should employ their arcane might to affect the Sleepers around them to most efficaciously Awaken all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">From time to time Psychonauts summon </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Taxi</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to aid them in furthering their understanding of the Supernal. Particularly experienced Psychonauts often maintain close relationships with these esoteric beings of raw conceptualization, sometimes going as far as to Name them anew.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">All Psychonauts bear an indigo tattoo of a glyph of a concept central to their spellcraft. While each Psychonaut\u2019s glyph is particular to her, the tattoos all signify a membership in the family of the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Azure Glyph</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Inks, dyes, berries, and materials that cause stains are important tools of their trade, allowing them to mark their passage through the places they\u2019ve passed on their voyages. Electrum coins, brass inkwells, wooden staves painted in brilliant colors and wand-like or feathery pens are all vital implements for those who walk the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Might</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. When Psychonauts prepare for war they gird themselves with rapiers, bows, and similar weapons of high precision.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Command &amp; Power</li> <li>Major Arcana: Mind &amp; Prime</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Fate</li> <li>Oracle: Chrysanthos</li> <li>Watchtower: The Azure Glyph</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Magician &amp; Strength</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Geniuses &amp; Monads</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Signum</li> <li>Yantras: Electrum coins, brass inkwells, dyes, berries, staining materials; Rapiers, bows, precision weapons<br /> <br /> Obrimos: Clerics &amp; Theurges on the Path of Enlightenment</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- A surprisingly large number of humanity\u2019s ancestral legends describe the activities of Obrimos. They have watched over the spiritual side of human beings since before the world\u2019s Fall. In those legends that focus on illuminating the inner processes of the human soul and dispelling ignorance, they are known by the name, Theurges. Far more legends describe individuals who employ their enlightened abilities as bastions that uphold the traditions, be they capricious and insular or liberal and dynamic, of the Sleeping masses around them and, in these tales they are known as Clerics.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Obrimos frequently cloth themselves in traditional garbs that allow them to move through the masses using the anonymity of familiarity. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The voudoun sets your offering of tobacco afire and utters your pray to the Loa. You miss the magic she has woven into the ritual and when your brother begins to recover from his alcoholism you ascribe it Their intervention. Perhaps your ignorance of the spell she has cast actually reinforces its power, its effects making themselves known in ways that you fully expect according to your spiritual traditions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The altar boy goes about his day-to-day tasks largely unnoticed by you. The candles are always lit and extinguished as prescribed by Church-law. The altar is always clean and the holy water basin is always full of clean and pure water. You remain completely ignorant to the subtle spells he ritually casts through his mandated movements. You ascribe the sanctum\u2019s beneficent effects on those who come each day to the holiness of the space itself and never suspect that it isn\u2019t the space that sets them at ease but rather the Mage who works within it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Obrimos Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Prime</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. The Aethereal forces that descend from the universe\u2019s innate divinity. The substance of the soul. The font from which true belief springs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prime</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the creative principle that allows Clerics to forge substance from nothingness. Its material essence flows through all things. Energy in its purest form. The hottest flame, the brightest light, the most powerful lightning. It is the wellspring from which every Cleric draws her strength. The final arbitration of purpose.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the supernal given form. It is the ethereal base from which the world was originally fashioned and to which it will inevitably return. True substance. The miraculous written out into the world. It is the bedrock that supports the faith that sustains every Cleric. The internal truth of all things. Identity from conformity to tradition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: In the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Aether</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> what comes before, during, and after life are one and the same. Practioners whose magic relies upon the concepts of change, where one thing becomes another, find that their spells falter and fail, for whatever a thing might be elsewhere it is always its purest form that is revealed within the supernal realm\u2019s confines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Mythology</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hierophant</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Temperance</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Faith, conformity, and tradition. Balance, patience, and purpose. Purity of substance and form. Prime motion. True belief. Enlightenment. Community.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Awakened Tarot, Obrimos are identified with the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hierophant</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Given to them is the secret knowledge of the true forms of all things. They deal in purified energies and materials both. Their mysteries are closely linked to </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Temperance</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. The Fallen World\u2019s truths can only be revealed by striking a balance between motive force and substance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Theurges sometimes call upon </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Angels</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to champion their causes. The most tradition-bound of their number sometimes yoke such entities into extended servitude for the sake of their communities. Such beings often advise, inspire, protect, and watch over the faithful. Occasionally they are even employed to destroy on the faithful\u2019s behalf.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Clerics employ bleached linens, distilled liquids and other perfected materials in their spellcraft. Each and every Obrimos bears a soft key fashioned from pure gold that unlocks the door leading into the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Golden Key</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Golden coins, steel cups, wands of petrified wood, and staves of carefully cultivated hardwoods are often employed as ritualistic tools by those walking the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Enlightenment</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. When called to defend their communities, Clerics often wield double-edged swords, spears, and other weapons associated with nobility. </span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Purity &amp; Faith</li> <li>Major Arcana: Prime &amp; Spirit</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Death</li> <li>Oracle: Obrimos</li> <li>Watchtower: The Golden Key</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Hierophant &amp; Temperance</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Cherubim &amp; Seraphim</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Aether</li> <li>Yantras: Golden coins, steel cups, petrified wood, bleached linen, perfected materials; Double-edged swords, spears, noble weapon<br /> <br /> Aethos: Soothsayers &amp; Witches on the Path of Doom</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Myths that describe Aethos often ascribe powers of insight and prophecy to them. Theirs is the burden of knowing that which is yet to come and exacting the price by which that knowledge is earned. They are known as Witches in those myths where they employ knowledge of the future for their own ends. More frequently though, myths paint them as Soothsayers who share their insights with all who are willing to listen to their mad ravings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soothsayers lead hidden lives and often dwell in rural locales. After millennia of persecution at the hands of others, most rarely share their knowledge.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The neighboring farmer was slow in sowing his fields this year. You thought he was merely being lazy but the late rains drowned most of the seeds you had planted. You never suspected that he saw patterns the weather and environment that you were beyond the patterns recorded in your almanac. You just chalk up his avoidance of the disaster to the luck of indolence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Everyone thinks that the class goth girl is crazy. You go so far as to actively make her life miserable, after all, conformity is an important part of growing up. You had it coming when she snarled back at you and pronounced a curse. You don\u2019t believe in such things though. You chalk up your stubbed toes and flat tires to simple bad luck, never realizing that the magic she used against you was very, very real.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Aethos Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcana</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fate</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. The Malic forces that record the shape of the future. The paths laid out before the traveler. The web of destiny. The end and the beginning. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the end of all things. Soothsayers use their knowledge of it to predict when endings are nigh. It is the all consuming force of oblivion that collects all to its breast. Tears shed from Cassiel\u2019s eyes. The one true door leading from what was to what will be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fate</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is the tangled skein of threads that chart out the courses of all things through their lives. Understanding its complex, multi-layered patterns give Soothsayers insight into paths that each thing inevitably walks. Every crossing, every meeting, and every parting can be found within destiny\u2019s weave. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Prime</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The labyrinthine expanses of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Malum</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are a dark and shadowed space where no fire can burn. Travelers must rely on the energy they bring with them to navigate its twisting passages and cavern-like expanses. Mages whose spells invoke the primal energies of the universe find that their magic operates at a tiny fraction of its normal power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Mythology</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">High Priestess</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wheel of Fortune</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Intuition, insight, and prophecy. Luck, karma, and destiny. Inevitability. The Collection of that which is due. Crossings, meetings, and partings. Departure from the familiar. Oblivion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Aethos are represented by the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">High Priestess</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> in the Awakened Tarot\u2019s arcana. Given to them is the fortitude of vision to pierce veils and resolve mysteries. A Soothsayer\u2019s intuition is her greatest asset. Aethos mysteries revolve around the workings of the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wheel of Fortune</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. They are privy to the Fallen World\u2019s cycles, both visible and invisible. It is through charting its revolving path that they can see the path that lies before them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soothsayers will occasionally summon </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Spectres </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">to aid them in charting destiny\u2019s byways. Echoes of things consumed by oblivion, Aethos treat with such creatures carefully lest they fall victim to the dark energies that course throughout their supernal substance. Particular daring or completely doomed Soothsayers sometimes go so far as to bind these entities into servitude.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Blood, fungi, and decaying things are the tools of a soothsayer\u2019s trade. A simple copper-bladed sickle is the badge of her allegiance to the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Copper Sickle</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Maps, charts, copper coins, bronze cauldrons, and brass astrolabes are important tools for the rituals and spellcraft employed by those walking the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path of Doom</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. When made to defend themselves, Soothsayers employ subtle weapons like poison or small weapons that are easily concealed like daggers and darts.</span></span></span><ul><li>Approach: Inevitability &amp; Collection</li> <li>Major Arcana: Fate &amp; Death</li> <li>Minor Arcana: Prime</li> <li>Oracle: Aethos</li> <li>Watchtower: The Copper Sickle</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The High Priestess &amp; The Wheel of Fortune</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Moirae &amp; Wraiths</li> <li>Supernal Realm: Malum</li> <li>Yantras: Copper coins, bronze cauldrons, brass astrolabes, blood, fungi, decaying materials; Daggers, darts, poisoned weapons</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><b><br /> <br /> The Pathless<br /> </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mavericks: Bards &amp; Savants with no Path</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Not all Mages Awaken to the well-defined track of a path. These Mavericks make do without the guiding tutelage of a mentor and literally blaze their own trails through the Supernal wilderness. Those that share the fruits of their difficult explorations with their fellow human beings are known as Savants in tales told by those they\u2019ve aided. The vast majority use the knowledge gained from flitting from one destination to the next for their own aggrandizement. People who cross paths with them, name them Bards.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Extraordinarily rare among the Awakened and oft-times confused for the Mad, Bards find it hard to fit in with the Sleepers that surround them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The chubby girl sitting in the coffee shop\u2019s corner listens to music all day long while she writes in her notebook. You\u2019ve already confused her for some kind of local poet. After all, it\u2019s a better explanation for why she constantly murmurs to herself and seems deep in thought. If you ever managed to look over her shoulder and glimpse the arcane truths she fills page after page with, one of you would certainly be institutionalized.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The middle-aged stock boy always has a far-away look in his eye. You think it makes him clumsy and error-prone and in a way it does. But you\u2019d collapse under the deluge of information he is constantly observing. If you knew the truth, that his mind travels afar, unshackled from a body that has been left to go through the automatic motions of a simplified life, your own grasp of reality would very likely unravel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Maverick Magic</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruling Arcanum</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>Bards Awaken to find themselves in the Supernal wilderness, far from the paths that lead to the ten known Watchtowers. The may select any one Arcanum of their choice as their one and only ruling Arcanum. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If at any time they find a master Mage willing to form a mentor/pupil relationship with them they replace their chosen ruling Arcanum with their mentor\u2019s ruling Arcana. This acts sets their feet on a specific Path which they cannot, thereafter, abandon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inferior Arcanum</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Since Bards wander back and forth across all of the Supernal Realms they do not suffer the disadvantage of possessing an inferior Arcanum. Should they ever find a mentor and, thereby, elect to trod one of the ten Paths they gain the disadvantage of that Path\u2019s inferior Arcanum becoming an inferior Arcanum for them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Adopting a Path</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Most Mages who Awaken as Bards have fierce independent streaks. It is not easy for them to enter into a mentor/pupil relationship with a master who walks one of the ten Paths. In addition to purchasing a dot of the Mentor merit to represent their new master, they must sacrifice a dot of Willpower. The master must expend a point of Willpower to seal the relationship and bind the pair in the sacred rights of tutelage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Selecting Arcana</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- During character creation, a Maverick\u2019s ruling arcanum may have from one to three dots. A generalist may distribute her starting Arcana dots evenly across six different Arcana (i.e., 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1) in addition to the other options. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols &amp; Myths</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-- </b>The </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fool</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tower</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Innocence, spontaneity, and freedom. Disaster, upheaval, and revelation. Experimentation and theft. Making one\u2019s own way through the world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While Mavericks do not walk a particular Path they still find representation within the Awakened Tarot through the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fool</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. They revel in their unbound ability to walk among all of the Supernal Realms and rely on their innocence to pilfer knowledge when it cannot be won through experience and experimentation. Their mysteries are bound by the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tower</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Wrestling one\u2019s way through the Supernal wilderness is not without risk and more than a few Bards end their careers as one of the raving Mad.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bards are not completely helpless amongst the warp and weft of the Supernal. Every Bard can call for </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernal Guides</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to help them make their way from one place to the next. Particularly wizened Bards or those who have mastered a great deal of Magic have been known to bind such entities to serve at their beck and call. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Even though Bards are relatively promiscuous with the materials they employ in their rituals and the tools they use to aid their spellcraft, each and every one of them maintains some form of personal journal representing the secret eleventh Watchtower, the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watchtower of the Hidden Tome</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to which no </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Path</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> leads. Every Maverick must find their own way to its seemingly empty halls. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Empty Legacy</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Bards may not learn Attainments. Since they are all self-taught, they have no Legacy to ascend to.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Orders</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- Note that Mavericks may still participate in Mage society as normal and benefit from membership in one of the Orders. They might also choose to forego such membership and dwell as one of the Nameless.</span></span><ul><li>Approach: Experimentation &amp; Theft</li> <li>Major Arcana: Any one</li> <li>Minor Arcana: None</li> <li>Oracle: None</li> <li>Watchtower: The Hidden Tome</li> <li>Awakened Tarot: The Fool &amp; The Tower</li> <li>Supernal Entities: Frastors</li> <li>Supernal Realm: any</li> <li>Yantras: any</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><b><br /> <br /> You're Doing It Wrong (or the Left-Handed Paths)<br /> </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While some practices like human sacrifice and ritualized abuse are obviously Left-Handed, there are those among all of the Paths that consider entire magical traditions to be subtly and inherently Left-Handed. This is because the threshold for abusive practice can be a blurry and ambiguous thing. More than a few Mages walking Gross Paths consider Subtle Paths, with their command over magics that interfere with the fate, mind, and spirit to be Left-Handed in nature. Similarly, some Mages walking Subtle Paths consider Gross Paths, which are all more than capable of shaping the physical world around them, to be Left-Handed in nature.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">These distinctions don\u2019t stop at the divide between Gross and Subtle Arcana. Some Awakened consider Paths that employ their Inferior Arcanum as a Major Arcanum to be Left-Handed. After all, there must be a reason why they are denied such powers while others use it freely. What else could it be other than the inherent wrongness in such spellcraft?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And there are many who deny that Mavericks wayfare across throughways off the known Paths and instead choose to believe that these masterless Awakened walk a dark Path that leads directly into the maw of the Abyss. To these Mages, being self-taught is, in itself, sign enough that one is walking a Left-Handed Path.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ultimately, while some magical practices are obviously Left-Handed, there is also a large grey area of practice that is left for individual Mages to decide whether or not they believe them to be Left-Handed in nature. Like walking a Path and learning from one\u2019s mentor, which practices fall into which categories is mostly a matter of personal perspective for the Awakened. And thus who is Left-Handed varies from Cabal to Cabal, Consilium to Consilium, and Caucus to Caucus.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:57:07-08:00","id":1186964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41818#post41818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's what I came up with on this.<br /> <br /> In this alternate cosmology, there are still five known Realms in the Supernal World; but each Realm has within it five Kingdoms, each with its own Watchtower. As such, there are 25 Paths to which a mage can Awaken. The Watchtowers presented in the corebook are considered the &quot;core&quot; of the Realm in question. The two primary Arcana of that Path are the dominating influences on the landscape. However, as you move away from that central point, the Gross Arcanum in that direction begins to influence the landscape, but the Subtle Arcanum still dominates.<br /> <br /> <b>Realm of the Aether</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Aether, the guiding principle is <i>Faith</i>. Faith can move mountains, change lives, and shine in the dark when all other lights have been extinguished. The inhabitants of the Aether will always try to encourage the mage to become that light, but one man\u2019s \u201clight\u201d is not always the same as his neighbor\u2019s. Some will take strength from their Faith and use it to reach for the greatest heights (Path of the Mighty). Some will use their Faith in the service others and give what they can for the greater good (Path of Sacrifice). Some will apply their Faith with the greatest of ease for the maximum effect, and find themselves rewarded (Path of Immortality). Some will use that Faith to unite that which is separated and forge chains to link them all together (Path of Unity). Some will simply ride the Universal Cycle with joy in their hearts and have Faith that they will see it through to the Great End (Path of Eternity).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Celestial Spheres<br /> Abode of Angels, Watchtower of the Gold Key<br /> <b>Obrimos:</b> the Theurges on the Path of Might<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Death<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of World Trees<br /> Abode of Dryads, Watchtower of the Oaken Sickle<br /> <b>Verbenae:</b> the Druids on the Path of Sacrifice<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Spirit<br /> With great trees stretching down into the mist and high into the clouds, the Kingdom of World Trees awaits those who would choose Sacrifice as the way to the heavens. Those who visit here will find themselves leaping among the branches and leaves, risking a fall at every step. The Dryads will not help the would-be mage; in fact, they will ask him for assistance. They will beg for water for their drying leaves, ask for help in removing vines and weeds from their tiny, tree-top gardens. Only those who stop and help, and can keep their balance, will be guided to the branches of a great oak. Through a door carved into the side in the shape of a sickle, they can enter the Watchtower and leave their name in this sacred grove.<br /> Relation to Center - Down<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Effortless Action<br /> Abode of Celestial Masters, Watchtower of the Jade Crucible<br /> <b>Athanatos:</b> the Alchemists on the Path of Immortality<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Fate<br /> Well below the crashing skies of the Aether is a series of furnaces and crucibles, surrounded by huts containing all manner of materials. Waiting here for the would-be mage are the Celestial Masters, willing to offer guidance to those who ask the right questions. Many have come here and begun to throw items into the crucibles and furnaces, hoping to forge themselves the right substance to grant them their wishes of power and immortality. Fewer still have known to search for the Jade Crucible, but this does not grant them the knowledge of the correct materials to use. Only by taking the time to study with one of the old Masters can one hope to find the way. Only by understanding how simple it really is will the Watchtower be revealed.<br /> Relation to Center - Under<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Divine Simplicity<br /> Abode of Sefirot, Watchtower of the Stardust Chain<br /> <b>Halusis:</b> the Geomancers on the Path of Unity<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Death<br /> Within the Realm of Aether, there exists a great chain, linking all the way up to the clouds. If one were to begin to ascend this chain, they would find more chains going off in other directions, and those links having yet more chains. If the would-be mage can take a step back to see, they will find those chains going in all directions, linking everything together in a massive web. At different points, many chains will link together in a seeming knot of connected things; all the chains for animals &amp; plants will connect as all things living, all the chains for lust and envy and wrath and greed will come together as a collection of vices. At the greatest nexus points are the Sefirot, representing the highest ideals and greatest concepts. By following the chains of the Sefirot, the would-be mage can climb this web to the Watchtower and leave their name on the wall of stardust.<br /> Relation to Center - Below<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Righteous Order<br /> Abode of Avatars, Watchtower of the Lotus Table<br /> <b>Ogygios:</b> the Channelers on the Path of Eternity<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Death<br /> On a great, calm pool of water, there are endless lotus blossoms, each floating upon the surface and dancing to their own tunes. Some of the blossoms will collect together and all dance in harmony. Others will separate after a long time of dancing together, and begin to drift away, or sink beneath the surface altogether. New blossoms will break the surface and begin to dance, either alone or with others. The would-be mage who comes here has no one and nothing to interact with, until they understand what they are seeing. Each blossom is a soul; each collection is a circle of friends and family. When they drift away or sink, the circle is broken. Death or disorder has taken someone away. When a new blossom appears, a new soul has entered the world. Once the Awakening soul has grasped this, an Avatar will join him and show him to the Watchtower.<br /> Relation to Center - Beneath</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of Arcadia</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Arcadia, the guiding principle is <i>Bravery</i>. As the old saying goes, \u201cFortune Favors the Brave.\u201d Dealing with Fate, in all its forms, requires a mage to take chances, face changes, and trust that the outcome will be what was meant to happen. Arcadia will test a would-be mage\u2019s mettle with warnings of danger, portents of doom, and threats of death; those who go on to face the tests and brave the dangers have better understanding of Fate and how it works for them, against them, and with them. Some will treat Fate as the coming storm, full of chaos and energy, but better for its passing (Path of Thunder). Some will see the winding up of living beings and happenstance and they will not hesitate to cut it when necessary (Path of Destiny). Some will see Fate as something that can be hammered and molded into shape, forcing it into a forged destiny (Path of Artifacts). Some will want to know all the paths Fate has laid out and see all the possibilities, even if it destroys their minds (Path of Discovery). Some will simply let the tides of Fate and Time push &amp; pull them where it will and trust to luck (Path of Thistle).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Enchantment<br /> Abode of the Fae, Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn<br /> <b>Acanthus:</b> the Enchanters on the Path of Thistle<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Forces<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Storms<br /> Abode of Great Ravens, Watchtower of the Frozen Spear<br /> <b>Magi:</b> the Wizards on the Path of Thunder<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Space<br /> The Watchtower of the Frozen Spear stands at the peak of the highest mountain of Arcadia, stretching above even the tallest tree of the greatest forest of the Realm, surrounded by vast seas of snow and ice. Perched upon its many peaks are the Great Ravens who call this region home. They wait for would-be mages to approach the Watchtower and bring down storms and clouds of black wings upon those who would enter. The path for anyone who could call themselves a wizard is difficult, and the Path of Foresight requires that a Wizard be prepared for hardship and sudden changes in fortune. If successful, a mage can carve their name into the handle of the Frozen Spear with one of the many icicles hanging from the arches of the tower\u2019s doorways.<br /> Relation from Center - Up<br /> <br /> Kingdom of the Turning Wheel<br /> Abode of the Norns, Watchtower of the Obsidian Knife<br /> <b>Moirae:</b> the Fate-Weavers on the Path of Destiny<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Matter<br /> As a would-be mage wanders through the forests of Arcadia, approaching the mountains takes the visitor through a region that is strange even by the standards of this Realm. At first, the trees appear to be a birch of some kind, with white bark and red leaves and vines. Upon closer inspection, they are found to be gigantic bones with the leaves and vines being pieces of flesh still attached to them. This is a place built on the bodies of Giants and Titans, cut up and stripped bare to make of Forest of Flesh &amp; Bone. The only inhabitants of this Kingdom are 3 women; call them Norns, Fates, or the Weird Sisters. It doesn\u2019t matter to them, but they will test a visitor before allowing entrance to the Watchtower. Passing the test grants the mage a pair of shears which they can use to hack their name into the thick, black walls of the Watchtower.<br /> Relation from Center - Across<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Mines<br /> Abode of Dwarfs, Watchtower of the Diamond Chisel<br /> <b>Techne:</b> the Craftsmen on the Path of Artifacts<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Space<br /> Doting the landscape of the Enchanted Forests of Arcadia are several great holes in the ground. These holes will lead to great caves and vast mines where the Dwarfs make their homes and craft their enchanted items. The Dwarfs have great smiths and forges working at all times, day and night are irrelevant under the ground. The powerful artifacts they create lie on rows and columns of shelves, well maintained and polished, but one stands out among all others \u2013 the Diamond Chisel. This tool must be taken before the would-be mage can continue, and the Dwarfs will only allow those who show some skill in crafting to take it with them. Once obtained, the visitor travels deep within one of the great caverns to the Watchtower, gleaming bright with clear crystal. When they have etched their name into the Watchtower with the Chisel, they can truly claim the title of Craftsman.<br /> Relation from Center - Below<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Revelation<br /> Abode of Nebulas, Watchtower of the Opal Door<br /> <b>Eureka:</b> the Astrologers on the Path of Discovery<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Matter<br /> High above, in the skies of Arcadia, lays the Boundless Firmament. In these endless reaches, all possibilities are waiting to be found. Each potential outcome is a pinpoint of light against a backdrop of black. Reaching for the stars here is not a metaphor, but a reality. Each star contains new knowledge, and with that knowledge comes the potential to know more and do more. Each new discovery leads to another, but that is another star to chase, another bright point for the Astrologer to follow, and they simply do not have the time. The Watchtower of the Opal Door, the brightest spot on the horizon, pulls potential mages in like a white dwarf star. Here, they must burn their name into the door before too long or fall back to earth, forever denied the Boundless Firmament again.<br /> Relation from Center - Above</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of Pandemonium</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Pandemonium, the guiding principle is <i>Purification</i>. The creatures of the Realm are there to expose the flaws of the soul and to force improvement within the soul. They tempt, they torture, they steal, they punish and they abuse; All in the name of turning the would-be mage into a soul worthy to hold the power of magic. Pandemonium will accept no weaklings or cowards. Some will be tempted to Glutton themselves and simply take what is given, but they must move on to find the Watchtower (Path of Determination). Some will be tempted with a Lust for everything a body could desire, but only by focusing will they find the Watchtower (Path of Introspection). Some will see the strength of other souls and Envy them and wish to Greedily take what they see, but only by forging their own soul will they find the Watchtower (Path of Forging). Some will be Prideful and try to hide their flaws, but if they will be open and lay bare, they will be admitted into the Watchtower (Path of Scourging). Some will find they are harassed and tempted to give into Sloth, but those who learn patience will discover the Watchtower (Path of Observance).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Nightmares<br /> Abode of Demons, Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet<br /> <b>Mastigos:</b> the Warlocks on the Path of Scourging<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Matter<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Abundance<br /> Abode of Harpies, Watchtower of the Bone Trident<br /> <b>Satur:</b> the Devoted on the Path of Determination<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Spirit<br /> Nestled in a valley in the Mountains of Abundance, the Watchtower of the Bone Trident sits. All the things one could ever want in life are there, piled in heaps to create this mountain range. Seemingly endless tracts of junk &amp; gadgets, food &amp; clothes, positions &amp; people make up the mountains. The mountains will rise and fall as their importance shifts based on the souls who travel through the mess. Would-be mages who travel here are free to dive within the mounds and take what they can when they can, but the Harpies who live atop these mountains are only too happy to teach them a lesson about what is truly precious \u2013 the soul. Anyone who grabs up the abundant materials lying about will find themselves in the clutches of a Harpie, carried far away from the Watchtower and dumped into another pile. Only those who can remain determined enough to go past all the garbage can finally be called a Devoted mage of the Bone Trident.<br /> Relation to Center - Above<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Temptations<br /> Abode of Sirens, Watchtower of the Banyan Staff<br /> <b>Askesis:</b> the Yogis on the Path of Introspection<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Matter<br /> Upon a rolling hill of dried grass, under an overcast sky, there\u2019s a series of tables and bed and chests, containing every manner of food, drink, pleasure and distraction created since the beginning of time; anything and everything someone could possibly desire to fulfill their bodily needs. Drifting across their Plain of Desire are the calls of the Sirens, telling the visitor to this Kingdom all about how great it will feel and how easy it is to give in to their temptations. Many a would-be mage has succumbed to their calls, and found himself back in the Fallen World, still hungry and unAwakened. For those who focus past all these temptations, beyond stands the Watchtower of the Banyan Staff, where a mage may carve their name into the trunks of the trees.<br /> Relation to Center - Across<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Transmutation<br /> Abode of Golems, Watchtower of the Copper Mallet<br /> <b>Telchines:</b> the Artificers on the Path of Forging<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Death<br /> Deep in the caves of Pandemonium is a forge like no other. Here, it\u2019s not metal that is worked, but souls. The visitor who is drawn here already knows their flaws, and wants them burned out or hammered out. He doesn\u2019t care, because he loathes those flaws, and wants the strength he sees in others. But the Golems do not give him what he wants, it must be earned. The would-be mage must place his soul upon the anvil, with mallet in hand, and perform the task himself. When a mage can forge his soul into the desired form, then can he approach the Watchtower to leave his name within its walls.<br /> Relation to Center - Under<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Distractions<br /> Abode of Goblins, Watchtower of the Marble Labyrinth<br /> <b>Perispao:</b> the Mystics on the Path of Observance<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Forces<br /> Contained within the Kingdom of Distractions are endless chambers filled with shining baubles, grating music, pungent smells, and rough surfaces. Many a would-be mage has lost his way completely in the continuing stretch of passages and chambers, too disoriented to tell which way he\u2019s been and which way is out. Adding to those distractions are the Goblins, who scurry about the passageways and through the various chambers tossing objects at the visitor, or destroying any attempts at marking their way. Those who can be patient, who can focus their minds and take their time, will eventually find the center of this maze. Within this waiting oubliette, the mage-to-be must slowly form their name in the walls with nothing more than their imagination.<br /> Relation to Center - Down</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of the Primal Wild</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of the Primal Wilds, the guiding principle is <i>Primitive</i>. Not in the sense of under-developed, but in the sense of being straight-forward and uncomplicated. The beings which exist here are clear and distinct about what they are and what they do. They don\u2019t talk in riddles, they don\u2019t play games, and they don\u2019t contemplate their nature. They exist as they are and they react to visiting souls within that paradigm: hunter or hunted, pack or herd, master or servant. Some will come to this Realm and see their place as a master of ephemera (Path of Authority). Some will come here and exalt in the headiness of a place full of life (Path of Ecstasy). Some will come here and form their own world out of the dirt (Path of Sculpting). Some will come to thrill in the hunt and the freedom to run over the open spaces (Path of Predators). Some will come here and bow down to the beings that live here, letting themselves be taken and open to everything (Path of Servitude).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Totems<br /> Abode of Beasts, Watchtower of the Stone Book<br /> <b>Thyrsus:</b> the Shamans on the Path of Ecstasy<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Mind<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Burning Sands<br /> Abode of Djinn, Watchtower of the Brass Torch<br /> <b>Exousi:</b> the Sorcerers on the Path of Authority<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Prime<br /> Within the ravished garden of the Primal Wild is the Kingdom of Burning Sands. The Djinn drift and fly through here, creating vast winds and sandstorms. Lightning splits the skies and thunder splits the ears almost constantly. The Djinn are angry at the ruins they are left. The would-be mage has but one option to deal with them \u2013 take command. Only a soul who is willing and able to control the Djinn will be able to see his way through the sand and find the Watchtower, burning his name into the walls with his command of the smokeless flames.<br /> Relation to Center - Higher<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Mud<br /> Abode of Gargoyles, Watchtower of the Clay Statue<br /> <b>Peitho:</b> the Binders on the Path of Sculpting<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Space<br /> In the damp earth of the Primal Wilds, the Gargoyles wait for a new creator. Each visiting soul encounters these creatures, waiting for orders or for the generative act to begin. The souls here seem compelled to create something out of the mud and clay around their feet. Once a would-be mage begins to create a new gargoyle, the others will turn their backs and guard, watching for any who would interfere with the creation process. The completed gargoyle must have life imbued into it, through the force of will of the Sculptor, binding it into servitude. Once this has been completed, the newly created gargoyle can be instructed to lead the way to the Watchtower, where it will claw its master\u2019s name into the walls.<br /> Relation to Center - Down<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Mountain Tundra<br /> Abode of Wendigo, Watchtower of Antler Bow<br /> <b>Necans:</b> the Hunters on the Path of Predators<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Life<br /> The Primal Wilds are host to vast, open reaches of mountain and arctic tundra, dotted with herd animals of many kinds: caribou, musk ox, mammoths, antelope, bison, moose, elk; anything capable of existing in the chilled reaches of this realm. Running across this Kingdom in great packs are the Wendigo, spirits who have turned to cannibalism and begun feeding on other spirits. Once, they were herd animals like the others here, then the first souls came and showed them how to hunt, and they were forever changed. Would-be mages attracted to this Kingdom are here to join in that hunt, drawing power from the spirits they bring down and consume. Once a soul has covered many, many miles and forged weapons of the hunt, they will find a great Watchtower to scratch their name into with an antler or stone weapon.<br /> Relation to Center - Across<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Great Rivers<br /> Abode of Loa, Watchtower of the Ivory Horse<br /> <b>Houngan:</b> the Mediums on the Path of Servitude<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Mind<br /> n a place where the waters of the Primal Wilds collect into rivers, there dwell spirits who do not feel the need to serve the souls who visit here, nor do they wish to work with them. These spirits see beyond there here and now; they see far off into the unwritten future or back into the well-worn past. The souls of the would-be mages that visit here are just drops of rain in the Great Rivers of time. The souls who come here are not the masters, they are the servants. The Loa, for all their knowledge, envy one thing: sensation. Those willing to give themselves over to the Loa, even for such a brief period as their Awakening, will find this moment stretched into an eternity. The Loa will take their time with the pleasures of sensation, but in the end, they will always leave the visiting soul at the foot of the Watchtower, where they may leave their name and claim the power they have earned with their servitude.<br /> Relation to Center \u2013 Beneath</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Realm of Stygia</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Within the Realm of Stygia, the guiding principle is <i>Acceptance</i>; Acceptance of one\u2019s fates, of their state of being, of their place in the Universe, of their flaws, and of themselves. Stygia accepts those who come to its Watchtowers with open arms, open hearts and open minds. The inhabitants of the Realm will never, ever interfere with a visitor\u2019s wanderings through the Realm. Neither will they guide, push, pull or direct anyone to a particular Watchtower. The soul of a mage in Stygia will drift until the natural pull of a Watchtower draws them in. Those who Awaken within Stygia have seen Death, and they understand it\u2019s place in the scheme of things, and they accept it as well as their own place. Some choose to fight, despite the knowledge of futility, but find nobility in the fight (Path of Strife). Some choose to help balance out the natural ebb &amp; flow between life &amp; death, loving each thing and crying at their passing (Path of Tears). Some concern themselves with the transition and transformation from one state to another, and help to ease that transition (Path of Doom). Some simply wait for the end, watching for signs and making their life as comfortable as possible in the meantime (Path of Oblivion). Some do their best to see what\u2019s coming and to either help it along or turn it aside, but they know that it is simply a matter of time (Path of Inevitability).<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Crypts<br /> Abode of Shades, Watchtower of the Lead Coin<br /> <b>Moros:</b> the Necromancers on the Path of Doom<br /> Supported by Matter, Opposed by Spirit<br /> See Tome of the Watchtowers<br /> Relation from Center \u2013 This is center<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Fallen Warriors<br /> Abode of the Valkyries, Watchtower of the Ebony Shield<br /> <b>Keres:</b> the Soul-Collectors on the Path of Strife<br /> Supported by Forces, Opposed by Life<br /> Towering above the Hall of Valhalla, placed upon the storm clouds of Odin, stands the Watchtower of the Ebony Shield, surrounded by constant mist and illuminated only by the lightning arcing though the clouds it stands on. Here, upon their winged steeds, the Valkyries spiral and swoop through the clouds and congregate within the tower, waiting for the next great warrior to enter and etch his or her name into the walls with their fine-tipped spears.<br /> Relation from Center - Above<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Autumn Fields<br /> Abode of the Blessed, Watchtower of the Garnet Apple<br /> <b>Koraie:</b> the Witches on the Path of Tears<br /> Supported by Life, Opposed by Spirit<br /> Among the rolling hills, covered in dried stalks of corn, red, gold and yellow leaves fall perpetually from the sky, despite the lack of trees. Here, the Great Lady of Life &amp; Death waits with her chosen few; souls which have achieved perfect balance with what they were and what they are. They stay here to help other souls pass through into what lays beyond, crying because they will miss those souls, but happy that they are going.<br /> Relation from Center - Over<br /> <br /> Kingdom of Crystal Caves<br /> Abode of Ghouls, Watchtower of the Quartz Spyglass<br /> <b>Asteri:</b> the Stargazers on the Path of Oblivion<br /> Supported by Space, Opposed by Mind<br /> Under Stygia lies the Timeless Ocean, but Stygia lies beneath all, concealed beneath rock. Within the rock, there are caves containing all manner of worldly riches. Within one cave lies a Watchtower which has tunneled through to the surface. Imbedded within the cave walls are crystals of all colors, glowing faintly, and within this cave, the ghouls wait. They wait for Oblivion. They look to the skies and stars for signs of death and destruction from above. Until that day, they greet those who enter this Kingdom with begging and pleading for answers, signs, and death.<br /> Relation from Center - Up<br /> <br /> Kingdom of the Timeless Ocean<br /> Abode of the Protogenoi, Watchtower of the Coral Goblet<br /> <b>Khresmoi:</b> the Soothsayers on the Path of Inevitability<br /> Supported by Time, Opposed by Matter<br /> Beneath the surface of Stygia lies the Timeless Ocean, the primordial depths beneath the waves where all things began and must eventually return. Within its depths is the stillness of eternity, the timeless pull of currents that were here before everything and will be here after we are dust. The sea breaks everything down; wears everything away, until nothing is left but the water. Floating with the currents of the sunless sea are the Protogenoi, beings formed when the world first began. They represent the most fundamental aspects of the world: life &amp; death, light &amp; dark, creation &amp; the void, earth &amp; sky. They alone resist the water\u2019s inevitable force, for now. They, too, will break down in the fullness of time. When the world has grown cold and dark, they will fall to pieces, too, and the cycle will begin again. Those who follow the Path of Inevitability come to know just how small and how fleeting they are, and have the utmost respect for the forces which spin the universe along.<br /> Relation from Center - Below </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>So, I have an idea that this is ONE way that the archmasters (on whose side is still up for debate, though obviously not the Aswadim and Tetrarchs, duh.) found a way of lessening the Abyss's influence over the Fallen World; by Ascending and then erecting a new Watchtower in a section of the Supernal that resonated most with them. Or possibly even creating Kingdoms separate from the original five, but then there's having to explain their organization and idk how I'd do THAT (heh I'm such a liar, I thought up an explanation while writing this) so I'll probably go with the former idea. Haven't decided if I want to completely nullify the Abyss, or just weaken it by a considerable amount. I don't hate if that much, and Paradoxes can be fun. Oh, sweet, sweet, Manifestations.<br /> (I have a special love for Abyssal entities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23877-obscure-sorcerer","user":"Obscure Sorcerer","date":". 02-17-2018, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23877-obscure-sorcerer","name":"Obscure Sorcerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}